<h2 id="part-a">Part A: Agreement</h2>
<h3 id="s1">1. Purpose &amp; Scope</h3>
<p>This Authorised Retailer Agreement &amp; Brand Standards (“Agreement”), establishes the terms, conditions and operating standards under which Apex Feeds AUST Pty Ltd (ABN 45 701 210 844) (“Apex Feeds”) supplies products to approved wholesale retailers (“the Retailer”) for resale to end consumers.</p>
<p>The purpose of this Agreement is to maintain consistent standards throughout the Apex Feeds authorised retail network and to protect the quality, safety, presentation and reputation of Apex Feeds products and brands.</p>
<p>By maintaining an approved wholesale account with Apex Feeds, the Retailer agrees to comply with the requirements of this Agreement relating to the purchase, resale, storage, handling, display, advertising and representation of Apex Feeds products, together with applicable requirements concerning customer complaints, product returns, quality concerns, product withdrawals and recalls.</p>
<h4 id="s1-1">1.1 Products Covered</h4>
<p>This Agreement, applies to all products, product ranges and brands manufactured, distributed or supplied by Apex Feeds to the Retailer, including products introduced or supplied after the commencement of this Agreement. Individual product ranges may be subject to additional storage, handling, display or other requirements contained within the Schedules to this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s1-2">1.2 Approved Retail Business</h4>
<p>Wholesale, approval is granted to the legal business entity identified in this Agreement and is not transferable to another person, business or legal entity. Where the approved Retailer operates multiple retail locations under the same legal business entity and ABN, the Retailer may sell Apex Feeds products from those locations without requiring a separate wholesale agreement for each location.</p>
<p>Wholesale approval does not extend to separately owned or operated businesses, businesses operating under a different ABN or legal entity, or other third parties, unless separately approved by Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s1-3">1.3 Online Sales</h4>
<p>An approved Retailer may advertise and sell Apex Feeds products through its own website or online store where that website is legitimately owned or operated by the approved Retailer and clearly represents the Retailer’s business.</p>
<p>Approval to sell online does not authorise the Retailer to resupply Apex Feeds products to other retailers, wholesalers, resellers or third parties. Requirements relating to online marketplaces, third-party sales platforms, advertising and authorised sales channels are set out elsewhere in this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s1-4">1.4 Retailer Responsibility</h4>
<p>The Retailer is responsible for ensuring that its owners, managers, employees and other persons acting on its behalf comply with the applicable requirements of this Agreement when handling, promoting or selling Apex Feeds products.</p>
<p>These standards apply across all authorised locations and sales channels operated by the Retailer.</p>
<h3 id="s2">2. Changes in Ownership, Control or Business Details</h3>
<p>The Retailer must notify Apex Feeds of any material change to the ownership, control, legal structure or operating details of the Retailer’s business.</p>
<p>Where the persons who owned or controlled the Retailer at the time of approval cease to own or control the business, the Retailer must notify Apex Feeds before any further wholesale orders are placed under the existing account, or as soon as reasonably practicable where prior notification is not possible.</p>
<p>Notification must include updated details reasonably requested by Apex Feeds, including the names and contact details of the new owners or authorised representatives and any changes to the Retailer’s legal entity, ABN, billing information, delivery locations or accounts-payable contact details.</p>
<p>Change of Ownership, Same Legal Entity Where ownership or control changes but the Retailer’s legal entity and ABN remain unchanged, the existing wholesale account may remain active subject to review by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may require the new owners or authorised representatives to confirm acceptance of the current Authorised Retailer Agreement &amp; Brand Standards and provide updated account and contact information before further orders are accepted.</p>
<p>A change of ownership does not invalidate amounts already owing by the Retailer or orders validly placed through the Retailer’s wholesale account. Change of Legal Entity or ABN Where operation of the business transfers to a different legal entity or ABN, the existing wholesale account does not automatically transfer to the new entity.</p>
<p>The new entity must notify Apex Feeds and may be required to complete a new wholesale application, provide relevant business information and enter into a new Authorised Retailer Agreement before wholesale supply continues.</p>
<p>Any outstanding amounts owed by the previous legal entity remain payable by that entity in accordance with the applicable trading terms and are not transferred merely because the business has changed ownership or operation.</p>
<p>Account Authority Following Ownership Changes The Retailer is responsible for ensuring that only persons authorised by the Retailer place orders or make changes to its Apex Feeds wholesale account.</p>
<p>Following notification of an ownership or control change, Apex Feeds may temporarily restrict ordering or account access while updated ownership, contact, billing and account-authority information is verified.</p>
<p>Orders placed through the Retailer’s account by persons represented to Apex Feeds as authorised representatives may be treated as orders of the Retailer, subject to applicable law.</p>
<p>Failure to notify Apex Feeds of a material ownership, control or entity change may result in the wholesale account being temporarily suspended until the Retailer’s current details and authority to trade have been verified.</p>
<h3 id="s3">3. Term &amp; Acceptance</h3>
<p>This Authorised Retailer Agreement &amp; Brand Standards (“Agreement”) becomes effective on the date it is signed by the Retailer and accepted by Apex Feeds AUST Pty Ltd (ABN 45 701 210 844) (“Effective Date”).</p>
<p>This Agreement remains in effect for the duration of the Retailer’s authorised wholesale relationship with Apex Feeds unless it is replaced, superseded or terminated in accordance with the provisions of this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s3-1">3.1 Acceptance of Agreement</h4>
<p>As a condition of obtaining and maintaining Authorised Retailer status, the Retailer must read, understand and agree to comply with this Agreement and all applicable Schedules, policies and standards forming part of this Agreement.</p>
<p>The Agreement must be signed by an owner, director, partner or other person with authority to enter into agreements on behalf of the Retailer.</p>
<p>By signing this Agreement, the Retailer confirms that:</p>
<ul>
<li>all information supplied to Apex Feeds in connection with its wholesale account is true and accurate to the best of its knowledge;</li>
<li>the person signing this Agreement has authority to enter into the Agreement on behalf of and bind the Retailer;</li>
<li>the Retailer has reviewed, understood and accepts the requirements contained within this Agreement; * the Retailer agrees to ensure that its relevant owners, managers, employees and representatives are made aware of and comply with the standards applicable to their duties; and</li>
<li>the Retailer understands that continued access to Apex Feeds wholesale supply is conditional upon maintaining the requirements applicable to an Authorised Retailer.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id="s3-2">3.2 Commencement of Wholesale Supply</h4>
<p> Execution of this Agreement does not, by itself, require Apex Feeds to accept any particular wholesale order or provide any particular product, quantity, credit facility or trading terms.</p>
<p>Wholesale supply may commence once the Retailer’s wholesale account has been approved by Apex Feeds and all information reasonably required to establish the account has been provided.</p>
<p>Individual wholesale orders remain subject to product availability, applicable wholesale trading terms and acceptance by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Approval of a wholesale account does not guarantee continued availability of any particular product, product range, quantity or delivery timeframe.</p>
<h4 id="s3-3">3.3 Continuing Agreement</h4>
<p>The Retailer is not required to enter into a new Agreement for each wholesale order, retail location or new Apex Feeds product range.</p>
<p>Unless otherwise agreed in writing, this Agreement continues to apply to all subsequent wholesale purchases made by the Retailer while its Authorised Retailer status remains active.</p>
<p>Where the Retailer operates multiple locations under the same approved legal business entity and ABN, this Agreement applies to all such locations in accordance with Section 2 of this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s3-4">3.4 Changes in Ownership or Control</h4>
<p>Where the ownership or control of the Retailer changes, the Retailer must notify Apex Feeds within thirty (30) days of the completion of the sale, purchase, transfer or other change in ownership or control of the business.</p>
<p>The notification must include updated information reasonably required by Apex Feeds to maintain and verify the wholesale account, including, where applicable:</p>
<ul>
<li>the names and contact details of the new owners;</li>
<li>authorised representatives and persons permitted to place wholesale orders;</li>
<li>accounts payable and billing contacts;</li>
<li>changes to business contact information;</li>
<li>changes to delivery or retail locations; and</li>
<li>any change to the legal business entity or ABN.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where ownership or control changes but the Retailer continues to operate under the same legal business entity and ABN, the existing wholesale account may continue subject to review and verification by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may require the new owners or authorised representatives to confirm their acceptance of the current Authorised Retailer Agreement &amp; Brand Standards before further wholesale supply is provided.</p>
<p>Where the sale, purchase or transfer results in the business being operated by a different legal entity or ABN, the existing wholesale account does not automatically transfer to the new entity.</p>
<p>The new legal entity must notify Apex Feeds and obtain approval before placing wholesale orders under or in connection with the previous Retailer’s account.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may require the new entity to complete a new wholesale application and enter into a new Authorised Retailer Agreement &amp; Brand Standards.</p>
<p>A change in ownership or control does not extinguish or otherwise affect outstanding amounts properly owed to Apex Feeds by the applicable legal entity.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may temporarily restrict wholesale ordering or account access where reasonably necessary to verify new ownership, account authority, billing information or the identity of the legal entity responsible for the account.</p>
<h4 id="s3-5">3.5 Updates to this Agreement and Retailer Standards</h4>
<p> Apex Feeds may periodically update its operational, product handling, storage, advertising, claims, branding or other retailer standards where reasonably required as a result of changes to products, packaging, manufacturing processes, safety requirements, legal or regulatory obligations, or the operation of the Apex Feeds wholesale program.</p>
<p>Where an update materially affects the Retailer’s obligations under this Agreement, Apex Feeds will provide the Retailer with at least thirty (30) days’ written notice before the change takes effect.</p>
<p>The thirty (30) day notice period does not apply where an earlier change is reasonably necessary for:</p>
<ul>
<li>product or customer safety;</li>
<li>product withdrawal or recall;</li>
<li>food or feed quality concerns;</li>
<li>compliance with a legal or regulatory requirement; or</li>
<li>another urgent circumstance where delaying implementation could reasonably create a safety, compliance or product-integrity risk.</li>
</ul>
<p>In these circumstances, Apex Feeds may require the relevant standard or instruction to take effect immediately or within another reasonable timeframe specified in the notice.</p>
<p>Updated product-specific requirements may be issued through revised Schedules, retailer notices or other written communications from Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Where a proposed change materially alters the fundamental commercial or contractual terms of the relationship between Apex Feeds and the Retailer, Apex Feeds may require the Retailer to acknowledge or accept the updated terms before continued wholesale supply.</p>
<h4 id="s3-6">3.6 Current Contact Information</h4>
<p> The Retailer must maintain accurate and current contact information with Apex Feeds throughout the term of this Agreement.</p>
<p>This must include an appropriate email address and contact person capable of receiving communications concerning:</p>
<ul>
<li>wholesale account matters;</li>
<li>orders and invoices;</li>
<li>changes to retailer standards;</li>
<li>product and storage information;</li>
<li>product-quality or safety notifications;</li>
<li>product withdrawals or recalls; and</li>
<li>other notices relating to the Retailer’s relationship with Apex Feeds.</li>
</ul>
<p>The Retailer must notify Apex Feeds of changes to its nominated contact information within a reasonable period.</p>
<p>Notices and updates issued by Apex Feeds to the most recent contact details provided by the Retailer will be regarded as having been sent to the Retailer’s nominated contact details, subject to applicable law.</p>
<h2 id="part-b">Part B: Wholesale Trading</h2>
<h3 id="s4">4. Wholesale Account Terms</h3>
<p>Wholesale accounts are provided exclusively to Retailers approved by Apex Feeds AUST Pty Ltd (ABN 45 701 210 844) and must be operated in accordance with this Agreement and the applicable wholesale trading terms.</p>
<p>Access to wholesale pricing, ordering facilities or credit arrangements is provided solely for the approved Retailer’s legitimate business operations and must not be transferred, shared or made available to another business or person.</p>
<h4 id="s4-1">4.1 Wholesale Account Ownership and Use</h4>
<p> A wholesale account is established in the name of the approved legal business entity and ABN identified by the Retailer.</p>
<p>The account may be used to purchase products for all authorised retail locations operated by that same legal entity in accordance with Section 2 of this Agreement.</p>
<p>The Retailer must not allow another business, separate legal entity, retailer, reseller or third party to use its wholesale account or wholesale pricing to purchase Apex Feeds products. Wholesale account privileges and pricing are not transferable.</p>
<h4 id="s4-2">4.2 Authorised Account Representatives</h4>
<p> The Retailer may nominate owners, directors, managers, purchasing personnel or other employees as authorised representatives of its wholesale account.</p>
<p>Authorised representatives may place orders and communicate with Apex Feeds regarding the Retailer’s account within the authority granted to them by the Retailer.</p>
<p>The Retailer is responsible for orders properly placed through its wholesale account by its authorised representatives.</p>
<p>The Retailer must notify Apex Feeds within a reasonable period where an authorised representative is no longer permitted to place orders or act in relation to the account.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may request reasonable verification of a person’s authority before accepting instructions concerning significant account, billing or ownership changes.</p>
<h4 id="s4-3">4.3 Wholesale Ordering Wholesale orders may be submitted through:</h4>
<ul>
<li>the approved Apex Feeds wholesale website or ordering portal; or</li>
<li>email directly to Apex Feeds through the nominated wholesale ordering contact.</li>
</ul>
<p>Apex Feeds may introduce or approve additional ordering methods from time to time. Orders placed through other channels are not considered accepted unless subsequently confirmed by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>The Retailer is responsible for reviewing product selections, quantities, delivery information and other order details before submitting an order.</p>
<h4 id="s4-4">4.4 Minimum Wholesale Order</h4>
<p>The minimum wholesale order is $250.00 excluding GST, freight and delivery charges, unless otherwise agreed in writing by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Freight charges do not contribute toward the minimum wholesale order value.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may establish different minimum order requirements for particular products, manufacturing orders or promotional programs where disclosed to the Retailer before the relevant order is accepted.</p>
<h4 id="s4-5">4.5 Order Acceptance and Product Availability</h4>
<p>Submission of a wholesale order does not constitute acceptance of that order by Apex Feeds. Orders remain subject to product availability, production capacity, account status and confirmation by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may reasonably decline or adjust an order where:</p>
<ul>
<li>insufficient stock is available;</li>
<li>the requested quantity cannot reasonably be supplied;</li>
<li>a product has been discontinued or temporarily withdrawn;</li>
<li>a product or pricing error has occurred;</li>
<li>the Retailer’s account requires verification;</li>
<li>payment required for the order has not been received; or</li>
<li>another circumstance reasonably prevents Apex Feeds from fulfilling the order as submitted.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where an order cannot be fulfilled as submitted, Apex Feeds will communicate with the Retailer regarding the affected products or quantities.</p>
<h4 id="s4-6">4.6 Payment Terms — New Wholesale Accounts</h4>
<p> All new wholesale accounts operate on a payment-before-dispatch basis. Unless Apex Feeds has expressly approved credit terms in writing, wholesale orders must be paid in full, including applicable freight and other agreed charges, before the order is dispatched. Payment history established with Apex Feeds does not automatically create an entitlement to credit facilities.</p>
<h4 id="s4-7">4.7 Eligibility for Wholesale Credit Terms</h4>
<p> A Retailer may become eligible to apply for wholesale credit terms after maintaining an active trading relationship with Apex Feeds for a minimum of six (6) months and successfully completing at least six (6) wholesale orders. Eligibility does not guarantee approval. Apex Feeds may consider the Retailer’s payment history, ordering history, account conduct, business information and other reasonable commercial considerations when determining whether credit facilities will be offered. Apex Feeds may, at its discretion, consider an application for credit terms before the standard eligibility period where appropriate.</p>
<h4 id="s4-8">4.8 Approved Credit Accounts</h4>
<p> Where approved in writing by Apex Feeds, the Retailer may be provided with an initial credit facility of up to $1,000.00 with payment terms of fourteen (14) days from the applicable invoice date.</p>
<p>The applicable credit limit represents the maximum outstanding balance permitted under the Retailer’s approved credit facility unless otherwise agreed in writing.</p>
<p>A Retailer must not place additional orders on credit where doing so would cause the approved credit limit to be exceeded unless Apex Feeds has authorised the transaction.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may reasonably review a Retailer’s credit facility based on payment history, account activity and commercial circumstances. A credit facility may be increased, reduced, temporarily suspended or withdrawn following review.</p>
<p>Withdrawal of a credit facility does not necessarily terminate the Retailer’s Authorised Retailer status, and Apex Feeds may instead require subsequent orders to be paid before dispatch.</p>
<h4 id="s4-9">4.9 Invoices and Responsibility for Payment</h4>
<p> Invoices will be issued to the legal entity holding the approved wholesale account. Where the Retailer operates multiple locations under the same legal entity and ABN, the Retailer remains responsible for payment of orders properly placed for those locations through its wholesale account.</p>
<p>Internal arrangements between the Retailer’s stores, managers, employees or departments do not alter the Retailer’s responsibility for amounts properly owing to Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s4-10">4.10 Order and Invoice Discrepancies</h4>
<p> The Retailer must inspect wholesale deliveries within a reasonable period after receipt. Any visible shortage, incorrect product, incorrect quantity, picking error or other readily identifiable discrepancy must be reported to Apex Feeds within three (3) days of receiving the order.</p>
<p>Claims should include the applicable invoice or order number and reasonable supporting information, including photographs where relevant. This reporting requirement does not limit any right or remedy that cannot lawfully be excluded or restricted.</p>
<p>Product defects, freight damage and other product-quality claims are subject to the more detailed procedures contained elsewhere in this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s4-11">4.11 Wholesale Pricing</h4>
<p> Wholesale prices are determined by Apex Feeds and may be provided through the wholesale ordering system, current wholesale price lists, quotations or other written communications.</p>
<p>Wholesale pricing may be reviewed and changed from time to time to reflect changes in production costs, ingredients, packaging, freight, supply conditions or other commercial factors.</p>
<p>The price applicable to an accepted order will ordinarily be the wholesale price confirmed for that order.</p>
<p>Where an obvious administrative, system or pricing error is identified before fulfilment, Apex Feeds will notify the Retailer and provide the opportunity to proceed at the correct price or cancel the affected item or order without penalty.</p>
<h4 id="s4-12">4.12 Overdue Accounts</h4>
<p> Where an approved credit account has an overdue undisputed balance, Apex Feeds may temporarily suspend further credit purchases or wholesale supply until the overdue amount has been paid or another arrangement has been agreed in writing.</p>
<p>Suspension for non-payment does not extinguish the Retailer’s obligation to pay outstanding invoices. Apex Feeds may require future orders to be paid in full before dispatch following repeated late payment or other material payment concerns.</p>
<h4 id="s4-13">4.13 Debt Recovery</h4>
<p>Where an amount properly owing to Apex Feeds remains unpaid after its due date and reasonable attempts to obtain payment have been unsuccessful, Apex Feeds may refer the outstanding account to a debt collection agency or other appropriate recovery service.</p>
<p>To the extent permitted by law and the terms applicable to the debt, Apex Feeds may seek recovery of reasonable external costs incurred in recovering overdue amounts.</p>
<p>Nothing in this clause prevents Apex Feeds from exercising other lawful rights available in relation to unpaid accounts.</p>
<h4 id="s4-14">4.14 Manufacturing, Special and Made-to-Order Products</h4>
<p> Where a wholesale order requires dedicated manufacturing, production, special packaging, unusual quantities or products not ordinarily held as finished stock, Apex Feeds may require:</p>
<ul>
<li>payment in full before manufacturing or production commences; or</li>
<li>payment of a specified production deposit before manufacturing or production commences.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where a production deposit is required, Apex Feeds will disclose the amount and applicable cancellation conditions to the Retailer before the Retailer commits to the order. A production deposit may be designated as non-refundable where it reasonably reflects production, ingredients, packaging, labour or other costs committed specifically to fulfilling the Retailer’s order, subject to applicable law.</p>
<p>Once manufacturing has commenced, cancellation or modification of a manufacturing or special order is subject to approval by Apex Feeds and may not be possible where costs have already been committed.</p>
<h4 id="s4-15">4.15 Cancellation Before Dispatch</h4>
<p>Requests to cancel or modify a standard wholesale order should be made as soon as possible.</p>
<p>Where an order has not yet been dispatched and has not entered a manufacturing or other non-recoverable fulfilment process, Apex Feeds may accept the cancellation or modification.</p>
<p>Manufacturing and special orders remain subject to Section 4.14.</p>
<h4 id="s4-16">4.16 Cancellation After Dispatch</h4>
<p>Once a wholesale order has been dispatched, the Retailer remains responsible for receiving the delivery. A request to cancel an order after dispatch does not require Apex Feeds to intercept or recall the shipment.</p>
<p>Where Apex Feeds agrees to accept the return of otherwise correctly supplied wholesale stock, the Retailer is responsible for:</p>
<ul>
<li>accepting the original delivery;</li>
<li>maintaining the products in accordance with all applicable storage and handling requirements;</li>
<li>arranging and paying for authorised return freight; and</li>
<li>ensuring the products are returned to Apex Feeds in unopened, unused, saleable condition.</li>
</ul>
<p>Any approved refund will apply to the eligible returned stock value only. Original freight charges and costs incurred by Apex Feeds in delivering the original order are not refundable for a retailer-initiated cancellation where Apex Feeds supplied the order correctly, subject to applicable law.</p>
<p>No refund will be processed until any product Apex Feeds has required to be returned has been received and its condition assessed.</p>
<h4 id="s4-17">4.17 Account Security</h4>
<p>The Retailer is responsible for taking reasonable steps to protect login credentials, passwords and other access information associated with its Apex Feeds wholesale account.</p>
<p>The Retailer must notify Apex Feeds promptly if it becomes aware of suspected unauthorised access to or use of its wholesale account.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may temporarily restrict account access or ordering where reasonably necessary to investigate suspected unauthorised activity or verify account authority.</p>
<h3 id="s5">5. Wholesale Pricing &amp; Commercial Terms</h3>
<p>Apex Feeds establishes wholesale pricing for products supplied to Authorised Retailers based on applicable production costs, product ranges, order quantities and otORFERfher commercial considerations. Access to wholesale pricing is provided solely for the Retailer’s approved business operations and remains subject to the terms of this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s5-1">5.1 Wholesale Price Lists</h4>
<p> Current wholesale pricing may be communicated to the Retailer through:</p>
<ul>
<li>the Apex Feeds wholesale website or ordering portal;</li>
<li>wholesale price lists;</li>
<li>written quotations;</li>
<li>promotional offers; or</li>
<li>other written communications issued by Apex Feeds.</li>
</ul>
<p>Wholesale prices may be updated from time to time and are not permanently fixed by this Agreement. Unless otherwise agreed in writing, the wholesale price applicable to an order will be the price displayed, quoted or otherwise confirmed by Apex Feeds at the time the order is accepted.</p>
<h4 id="s5-2">5.2 Gst</h4>
<p>All Apex Feeds wholesale product prices are quoted exclusive of Goods and Services Tax (GST) unless expressly stated otherwise. GST will be calculated at the applicable rate and added to the wholesale product value, freight charges and any other taxable supplies at the time of invoicing.</p>
<p>The Retailer is responsible for payment of the GST amount shown on the applicable invoice in addition to the GST-exclusive wholesale price. Apex Feeds will provide tax invoices in accordance with applicable Australian taxation requirements.</p>
<p>Any wholesale price lists, quotations, promotional pricing or other commercial pricing issued by Apex Feeds should be interpreted as exclusive of GST unless expressly identified as GST-inclusive</p>
<h4 id="s5-3">5.3 Changes to Wholesale Pricing</h4>
<p> Apex Feeds may review and adjust wholesale pricing from time to time in response to changes including, but not limited to:</p>
<ul>
<li>ingredient and raw material costs;</li>
<li>livestock, insect or food-production costs;</li>
<li>packaging costs;</li>
<li>manufacturing and labour costs;</li>
<li>freight and logistics costs;</li>
<li>supplier pricing;</li>
<li>regulatory or compliance costs; and</li>
<li>broader commercial or market conditions.</li>
</ul>
<p>Changes to wholesale pricing apply prospectively and do not alter the price of an order already accepted by Apex Feeds unless otherwise agreed with the Retailer.</p>
<p>Where reasonably practicable, Apex Feeds will provide Authorised Retailers with advance notice of significant changes to standard wholesale pricing.</p>
<h4 id="s5-4">5.4 Individual Quotations</h4>
<p> Apex Feeds may provide individual written quotations for large-volume purchases, special orders, manufacturing orders or other non-standard requirements.</p>
<p>A quotation may specify:</p>
<ul>
<li>the applicable wholesale price;</li>
<li>quantities;</li>
<li>freight or delivery arrangements;</li>
<li>deposit or prepayment requirements;</li>
<li>production requirements;</li>
<li>validity period; and</li>
<li>other conditions specific to the proposed order.</li>
</ul>
<p>A quotation does not require Apex Feeds to supply the quoted goods after the quotation has expired. Where a quotation contains terms specific to an order, those terms apply to that order together with this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s5-5">5.5 Volume Pricing and Commercial Arrangements</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may offer different wholesale pricing, volume discounts, promotional pricing or other commercial arrangements to Retailers based on reasonable commercial factors including:</p>
<ul>
<li>order volume;</li>
<li>purchasing frequency;</li>
<li>product quantities;</li>
<li>promotional programs;</li>
<li>freight or distribution arrangements;</li>
<li>long-term trading relationships; or</li>
<li>other legitimate commercial considerations.</li>
</ul>
<p>The existence of a pricing or commercial arrangement with one Retailer does not automatically entitle another Retailer to the same arrangement. Any special pricing applies only for the period or circumstances for which it was offered and does not permanently modify the Retailer’s standard wholesale pricing unless confirmed in writing by Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s5-6">5.6 Wholesale Promotions</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may periodically offer wholesale promotions, introductory offers, quantity discounts, product bundles or other incentives. Promotional offers may be subject to specified:</p>
<ul>
<li>commencement and expiry dates;</li>
<li>minimum quantities;</li>
<li>eligible products;</li>
<li>participating Retailers;</li>
<li>stock availability; or</li>
<li>other reasonable promotional conditions.</li>
</ul>
<p>Promotional pricing does not establish an ongoing entitlement to purchase products at the promotional price after the promotion has ended.</p>
<h4 id="s5-7">5.7 Pricing 
Errors</h4>
<p>Where an obvious pricing, administrative, typographical or system error occurs, Apex Feeds may correct the error before fulfilling the affected order. Where the correction increases the amount payable, the Retailer will be informed and given the opportunity to:</p>
<ul>
<li>proceed with the affected product or order at the corrected price; or</li>
<li>cancel the affected product or order without penalty.</li>
</ul>
<p>Apex Feeds will not substitute a higher price after an order has been accepted merely because Apex Feeds subsequently changes its standard wholesale pricing.</p>
<h4 id="s5-8">5.8 Freight and Delivery Charges</h4>
<p>Wholesale product pricing does not include freight or delivery charges unless expressly stated otherwise. Applicable wholesale freight charges will be added separately to the order.</p>
<p>Freight charges do not contribute toward the $250.00 minimum wholesale order value established under Section 4 of this Agreement. Detailed freight, dispatch and delivery requirements are contained elsewhere in this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s5-9">5.9 Confidentiality of Wholesale Pricing</h4>
<p>Wholesale price lists, wholesale account pricing, non-public volume discounts, retailer-specific quotations, credit arrangements and other non-public commercial terms supplied by Apex Feeds are provided for the Retailer’s internal business use.</p>
<p>The Retailer must not knowingly distribute or publish confidential Apex Feeds wholesale pricing or retailer-specific commercial information to the general public or unrelated third parties. This does not prevent the Retailer from providing relevant information to its employees, accountants, professional advisers or other persons who reasonably require the information for the operation or administration of the Retailer’s business.</p>
<p>Nothing in this clause prevents disclosure where required by law.</p>
<h4 id="s5-10">5.10 No Authority to Set Terms for Other Retailers</h4>
<p>A Retailer has no authority to negotiate, advertise, represent or establish wholesale prices or commercial terms on behalf of Apex Feeds for another business. Authorised Retailers must not represent themselves as wholesalers, distributors or agents of Apex Feeds unless Apex Feeds has separately provided written authorisation for that role.</p>
<h3 id="s6">6. Recommended Retail Pricing &amp; Brand Positioning</h3>
<p>Apex Feeds may establish and publish a Recommended Retail Price (“RRP”) for products supplied through its Authorised Retailer network.</p>
<p>The RRP is intended to provide Retailers with guidance regarding the positioning and recommended consumer price of Apex Feeds products and to support consistent communication of product value across the Australian retail market.</p>
<p>All RRPs issued by Apex Feeds are recommendations only. The Retailer remains independently responsible for determining the prices at which it advertises and sells Apex Feeds products.</p>
<h4 id="s6-1">6.1 Recommended Retail Price</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may communicate current RRPs through:</p>
<ul>
<li>product price lists;</li>
<li>the Apex Feeds website;</li>
<li>wholesale ordering systems;</li>
<li>product catalogues;</li>
<li>promotional material;</li>
<li>product packaging; or</li>
<li>other written communications.</li>
</ul>
<p>Unless expressly stated otherwise, any retail price communicated by Apex Feeds to an independent Retailer is a recommended price only and there is no obligation upon the Retailer to comply with that recommendation.</p>
<h4 id="s6-2">6.2 Independent Retail Pricing</h4>
<p>The Retailer independently determines the final retail price at which Apex Feeds products are advertised and sold. Nothing in this Agreement requires the Retailer to sell or advertise Apex Feeds products at or above the RRP.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds will not withhold wholesale supply, withdraw an otherwise applicable wholesale benefit, or take disciplinary action against a Retailer merely because the Retailer independently chooses to advertise or sell an Apex Feeds product below its RRP.</p>
<h4 id="s6-3">6.3 Changes to Recommended Retail Pricing</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may review and update RRPs from time to time in response to changes in:</p>
<ul>
<li>wholesale pricing;</li>
<li>production and ingredient costs;</li>
<li>packaging;</li>
<li>product positioning;</li>
<li>product size or formulation;</li>
<li>market conditions; or</li>
<li>other relevant commercial considerations.</li>
</ul>
<p>Updated RRPs may be communicated to Authorised Retailers through revised price lists, wholesale communications or other appropriate channels. Changes to an RRP do not determine or restrict the Retailer’s independently established resale price.</p>
<h4 id="s6-4">6.4 Retail Promotions and Discount Advertising</h4>
<p>Retailers may independently conduct promotions or discount Apex Feeds products. Where the Retailer advertises a promotion, discount, saving or comparison involving an Apex Feeds product, the Retailer is responsible for ensuring that the advertising is accurate, not misleading or deceptive, and complies with applicable Australian consumer laws.</p>
<p>The Retailer must not falsely represent that:</p>
<ul>
<li>a discount or promotion has been authorised, funded or conducted by Apex Feeds where it has not;</li>
<li>Apex Feeds has established a particular promotional retail price where it has not;</li>
<li>a Retailer-specific promotion is an Australia-wide Apex Feeds promotion;</li>
<li>Apex Feeds is responsible for a discount independently offered by the Retailer; or</li>
<li>an advertised saving, previous price or RRP is inaccurate or misleading.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id="s6-5">6.5 Apex Feeds Promotions</h4>
<p>From time to time Apex Feeds may conduct or invite Authorised Retailers to participate in national, regional or retailer-specific promotional campaigns. Where a Retailer elects to participate in an Apex Feeds promotional campaign, it must accurately represent the applicable promotion and comply with any reasonable conditions relating to the use of Apex Feeds promotional materials, campaign dates, product eligibility and brand presentation.</p>
<p>Participation in an Apex Feeds promotional campaign does not prevent the Retailer from independently determining its resale prices, except to the extent otherwise lawfully permitted.</p>
<h4 id="s6-6">6.6 Brand Positioning</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds products must be represented professionally and in a manner that does not mislead customers regarding the nature, quality, quantity, origin or characteristics of the products.</p>
<p>Retailers must not use pricing, promotional or advertising material in a manner that:</p>
<ul>
<li>falsely represents the value, size, contents or characteristics of an Apex Feeds product;</li>
<li>creates a false or misleading impression that a promotion is operated or endorsed by Apex Feeds;</li>
<li>materially alters Apex Feeds supplied advertising material in a way that misrepresents the product or brand;</li>
<li>uses inaccurate product descriptions, claims or imagery; or</li>
<li>otherwise breaches the advertising and brand standards contained within this Agreement. Detailed requirements concerning the use of Apex Feeds branding, product imagery, social-media content and advertising materials are contained in the applicable Brand &amp; Advertising sections and Schedules of this Agreement.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id="s6-7">6.7 Product Bundles and Multi-Buy Promotions</h4>
<p>Retailers may include Apex Feeds products in independently created bundles, multi-buy offers or other retail promotions provided that:</p>
<ul>
<li>individual Apex Feeds products remain identifiable;</li>
<li>original product packaging and labelling are not removed, obscured or altered;</li>
<li>the promotion does not falsely imply Apex Feeds sponsorship or endorsement;</li>
<li>products are not repackaged or divided without written authorisation from Apex Feeds; and</li>
<li>any representations made regarding the products remain accurate.</li>
</ul>
<p>Nothing in this clause restricts the Retailer’s ability to independently determine the retail price of the bundle or promotion.</p>
<h4 id="s6-8">6.8 Price Representation</h4>
<p>Where a Retailer refers to an Apex Feeds RRP in advertising or promotional material, the RRP used must be the current RRP communicated by Apex Feeds for that product.</p>
<p>The Retailer must not knowingly use an outdated or inflated RRP to create a false or misleading impression of a greater discount or saving. The Retailer remains responsible for ensuring that any price comparison, savings claim or promotional representation complies with applicable Australian consumer law.</p>
<h3 id="s7">7. Freight, Dispatch &amp; Delivery</h3>
<p>Apex Feeds aims to provide reliable and appropriate freight services to Authorised Retailers while maintaining the quality, safety and integrity of products throughout transport. Freight methods, dispatch schedules and delivery arrangements may vary depending on the product type, destination, order size and environmental conditions.</p>
<p>The Retailer acknowledges that live feeder insects, frozen foods and other temperature-sensitive products require additional freight and handling considerations and may be subject to different dispatch arrangements from shelf-stable products.</p>
<h4 id="s7-1">7.1 Standard Wholesale Freight Rates</h4>
<p>Unless otherwise quoted or agreed in writing, standard wholesale orders containing non-perishable products are subject to the following flat-rate freight charges.</p>
<p>All freight charges are exclusive of GST unless expressly stated otherwise. Freight charges are separate from product value and do not contribute toward the minimum wholesale order requirement established under Section 4.</p>
<p>The above flat-rate freight charges apply to standard wholesale freight only and do not automatically apply to frozen products, unusually large or heavy consignments, palletised freight, special delivery requirements or other non-standard shipments.</p>
<p>Where an order requires non-standard freight, Apex Feeds will advise the Retailer of the applicable freight arrangements before dispatch.</p>
<h4 id="s7-2">7.2 Changes to Freight Rates</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may review and adjust its standard flat-rate freight charges where reasonably necessary due to changes in carrier pricing, fuel costs, freight networks, packaging requirements or other logistics costs. Current applicable freight charges will be made available to the Retailer through the wholesale ordering system, wholesale price lists or other written communications.</p>
<p>Where reasonably practicable, Apex Feeds will provide advance notice of significant changes to its standard wholesale freight rates.</p>
<h4 id="s7-3">7.3 Standard Non-Perishable Orders</h4>
<p>Shelf-stable, dry and other non-perishable wholesale products may be dispatched Monday to Friday, excluding public holidays and other periods where freight services are unavailable or unsuitable.</p>
<p>Standard wholesale orders will generally require approximately one (1) to three (3) business days for processing prior to dispatch. Processing and dispatch timeframes are estimates only unless Apex Feeds has expressly agreed to a particular delivery or dispatch date in writing.</p>
<h4 id="s7-4">7.4 Live and Frozen Product Dispatch</h4>
<p>Live feeder insects and frozen products are ordinarily dispatched on Mondays and Tuesdays to reduce the risk of consignments being held within freight networks over weekends. The standard order cut-off for live and frozen dispatch is 1:00 pm Sunday for the applicable week’s scheduled dispatch.</p>
<p>Orders received after the applicable cut-off may be held until the following suitable dispatch period. Live and frozen orders will generally require approximately one (1) to two (2) business days for processing, subject to stock availability, production requirements, freight availability and suitable shipping conditions.</p>
<p>Eligible locations within New South Wales may, at the discretion of Apex Feeds, be offered Wednesday dispatch where the destination, expected freight timeframe and prevailing conditions are considered suitable. Wednesday dispatch is not guaranteed and remains subject to the applicable 1:00 pm Sunday cut-off unless otherwise agreed by Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s7-5">7.5 Frozen Product Orders and Freight</h4>
<p> Frozen wholesale orders must be placed directly by email with Apex Feeds and are not covered by the standard state-based flat-rate freight schedule.</p>
<p>Freight for frozen products will be assessed and quoted individually based on factors including:</p>
<ul>
<li>destination;</li>
<li>order volume and weight;</li>
<li>packaging requirements;</li>
<li>available freight services;</li>
<li>expected transit time; and</li>
<li>temperature-control requirements.</li>
</ul>
<p>Apex Feeds may elect to subsidise part or all of the freight cost associated with a frozen wholesale order based on order value, volume, quantity or other commercial considerations. Any freight subsidy is provided at the discretion of Apex Feeds and does not create an ongoing entitlement to subsidised freight on future orders.</p>
<p>The applicable freight cost will be communicated to the Retailer before the frozen order is confirmed.</p>
<h4 id="s7-6">7.6 Direct Delivery by Apex Feeds</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may offer direct delivery to Retailers within Sydney and other serviceable locations in New South Wales where operationally practical.</p>
<p>Direct delivery is subject to:</p>
<ul>
<li>location;</li>
<li>order size;</li>
<li>applicable delivery charges;</li>
<li>existing delivery routes;</li>
<li>Apex Feeds’ production and operational workload; and</li>
<li>availability at the requested time.</li>
</ul>
<p>Direct delivery is provided by prior arrangement only and does not constitute an on-demand or guaranteed delivery service.</p>
<p>The Retailer should not assume that Apex Feeds can accommodate a particular delivery date or time until that arrangement has been expressly confirmed. Where a direct-delivery charge applies, the Retailer will be advised before the delivery arrangement is confirmed.</p>
<h4 id="s7-7">7.7 Delivery Address and Receiving Goods</h4>
<p>The Retailer is responsible for providing complete and accurate delivery information. The Retailer must notify Apex Feeds of any change to its delivery details before dispatch of the affected order. Where practical, the Retailer should ensure that an appropriate person is available to receive live, frozen or other temperature-sensitive deliveries.</p>
<p>Additional freight, redelivery or handling costs resulting from an incorrect address, inaccessible premises, refusal of a correctly supplied delivery or other circumstances within the Retailer’s reasonable control may be charged to the Retailer.</p>
<h4 id="s7-8">7.8 Inspection of Standard Deliveries</h4>
<p>The Retailer must inspect wholesale deliveries promptly after receipt. Visible shortages, incorrect products, incorrect quantities, picking errors or readily identifiable freight damage must be reported to Apex Feeds within three (3) days of receiving the order.</p>
<p>Claims should include:</p>
<ul>
<li>the relevant order or invoice number;</li>
<li>details of the affected product;</li>
<li>quantity affected;</li>
<li>photographs of the product and packaging where relevant; and</li>
<li>any other information reasonably required to investigate the claim.</li>
</ul>
<p>The Retailer should retain affected products and packaging until Apex Feeds advises whether they are required for inspection or return.</p>
<h4 id="s7-9">7.9 Live and Frozen Delivery Inspection</h4>
<p>Live and frozen products must be inspected immediately upon delivery. Where a Retailer believes a live or frozen shipment has been materially compromised during freight, the Retailer must notify Apex Feeds as soon as reasonably practicable and provide appropriate photographic or other evidence.</p>
<p>Affected products must not be discarded until Apex Feeds has been given a reasonable opportunity to assess the claim or has instructed the Retailer that disposal is permitted. Where frozen products are believed to have been materially thawed or otherwise temperature compromised, the Retailer must isolate the affected stock and must not offer it for sale until its suitability has been determined.</p>
<p>Detailed live-arrival and frozen-product claim requirements may be contained within the applicable Product Storage, Handling and Claims Schedules.</p>
<h4 id="s7-10">7.10 Freight Damage</h4>
<p>Damage to an external shipping carton does not, by itself, establish that the products contained within the shipment are damaged or unsuitable for sale. Where freight damage is claimed, Apex Feeds may require photographs showing:</p>
<ul>
<li>the external shipping carton;</li>
<li>freight or shipping label;</li>
<li>internal packaging;</li>
<li>location and nature of the damage; and</li>
<li>affected individual products.</li>
</ul>
<p>Apex Feeds will assess claims based on the condition of the products and the circumstances of the shipment.</p>
<h4 id="s7-11">7.11 Delayed or Lost Freight</h4>
<p>Where an order is delayed or believed to have been lost within a freight network, Apex Feeds will make reasonable enquiries with the applicable freight provider. A shipment will not automatically be considered lost solely because it has not arrived within an estimated delivery timeframe.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds must be provided a reasonable opportunity to investigate, trace or otherwise resolve the shipment with the freight provider before a replacement, credit or other remedy is determined. Nothing in this clause limits rights or remedies that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
<h4 id="s7-12">7.12 Extreme Weather and Unsafe Shipping Conditions</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may delay the dispatch of live feeder insects, frozen products or other temperature-sensitive goods where weather conditions or other environmental circumstances are reasonably considered likely to compromise animal welfare, product quality or the safe delivery of the order.</p>
<p>Relevant circumstances may include:</p>
<ul>
<li>extreme heat;</li>
<li>extreme cold;</li>
<li>severe storms;</li>
<li>flooding;</li>
<li>bushfires;</li>
<li>cyclones;</li>
<li>natural disasters;</li>
<li>significant freight-network disruption; or</li>
<li>dangerous conditions affecting the dispatch location, delivery destination or expected freight route.</li>
</ul>
<p>Apex Feeds may consider both the conditions at the point of dispatch and the forecast conditions expected during transit and at the delivery destination when determining whether a shipment should proceed.</p>
<p>Where dispatch is delayed under this clause, the delay will not constitute a failure by Apex Feeds to meet its ordinary processing or dispatch timeframe. Apex Feeds will endeavour to dispatch the affected order at the next reasonably suitable opportunity once conditions permit.</p>
<p>The welfare of live feeder insects and the integrity of temperature-sensitive products take priority over ordinary dispatch schedules.</p>
<h4 id="s7-13">7.13 Carrier and Freight Service Selection</h4>
<p>Unless otherwise agreed, Apex Feeds may select the freight provider and freight service considered appropriate for the products, destination and delivery requirements of the order. Apex Feeds does not guarantee the performance or delivery timeframe of an independent freight provider but will take reasonable steps to select appropriate freight services and assist with legitimate freight enquiries or claims.</p>
<h4 id="s7-14">7.14 Refused or Unaccepted Deliveries</h4>
<p>Where a Retailer refuses or fails to accept a correctly supplied wholesale delivery without a valid product-quality, freight or order-related reason, the Retailer may be responsible for reasonable costs arising from that refusal or failure to receive the shipment.</p>
<p>These costs may include original freight, return freight, redelivery charges and, where applicable, loss of products that cannot reasonably be returned to saleable stock due to the Retailer’s refusal or failure to receive them. Live, frozen or otherwise perishable products may not be eligible for return where their condition or safety can no longer reasonably be verified.</p>
<h4 id="s7-15">7.15 Responsibility Following Delivery</h4>
<p>Following successful delivery, the Retailer is responsible for storing, handling and maintaining Apex Feeds products in accordance with the applicable Product Storage &amp; Handling requirements contained within this Agreement and its Schedules.</p>
<p>Products that are subsequently damaged, contaminated, thawed, improperly stored or otherwise compromised while under the Retailer’s control may not qualify for credit or replacement where the issue was not caused by Apex Feeds or the freight process.</p>
<h3 id="s8">8. Authorised Sales Channels</h3>
<p>Apex Feeds wholesale approval authorises the Retailer to purchase Apex Feeds products for resale to end consumers through the Retailer’s own approved retail business and associated sales channels.</p>
<p>Authorised Retailer status does not grant the Retailer unrestricted distribution rights, wholesale distribution rights or authority to supply Apex Feeds products through third-party marketplaces or unrelated businesses.</p>
<p>The Retailer remains responsible for ensuring that all sales, advertising and distribution of Apex Feeds products comply with this Agreement, applicable Brand Standards and all relevant laws and regulatory requirements.</p>
<h4 id="s8-1">8.1 Physical Retail Stores</h4>
<p>The Retailer may sell Apex Feeds products from physical retail locations owned and operated by the approved legal entity. Where the Retailer operates multiple physical locations under the same legal entity and ABN, Apex Feeds products may be sold from those locations subject to each location complying with this Agreement and applicable product storage, handling and presentation requirements.</p>
<p>The Retailer must keep Apex Feeds reasonably informed of the physical retail locations operating under its wholesale account. A separately owned business, franchisee, licensee or business operating under a different legal entity or ABN is not automatically authorised by the Retailer’s wholesale approval.</p>
<h4 id="s8-2">8.2 Retailer’s Own Website</h4>
<p>The Retailer may advertise and sell Apex Feeds products through a website genuinely owned or operated by the approved Retailer and associated with the Retailer’s own business or trading identity. The Retailer’s website must clearly identify the Retailer as the seller of the products and must not create a false or misleading impression that the website is owned, operated or endorsed by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>The Retailer remains responsible for:</p>
<ul>
<li>accurate product descriptions and representations;</li>
<li>appropriate use of Apex Feeds branding and product imagery;</li>
<li>customer service relating to purchases made through its website;</li>
<li>appropriate storage and fulfilment of products;</li>
<li>compliance with destination-specific requirements; and</li>
<li>compliance with applicable Australian consumer and retail laws.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id="s8-3">8.3 Social Media</h4>
<p>The Retailer may advertise and promote Apex Feeds products through official social-media accounts operated for the Retailer’s business, including Facebook and Instagram.</p>
<p>Retailers may use:</p>
<ul>
<li>advertising and promotional material supplied or approved by Apex Feeds;</li>
<li>official Apex Feeds product photographs and information made available for retailer use; and</li>
<li>photographs, videos and other content independently created by the Retailer featuring Apex Feeds products within its own store or business.</li>
</ul>
<p>Retailer-created content must accurately represent Apex Feeds products and must comply with the advertising, product-claim and Brand Standards contained within this Agreement.</p>
<p>The Retailer must not materially alter Apex Feeds supplied artwork, product information or advertising material in a manner that creates an inaccurate or misleading representation of the product or Apex Feeds brand.</p>
<h4 id="s8-4">8.4 Third-Party Marketplaces</h4>
<p>Authorised Retailer status does not authorise the Retailer to advertise, list or sell Apex Feeds products through third-party online marketplaces.</p>
<p>This includes, but is not limited to:</p>
<ul>
<li>eBay; * Amazon;</li>
<li>Facebook Marketplace;</li>
<li>Catch; and</li>
<li>other third-party marketplace, auction or multi-seller platforms.</li>
</ul>
<p>Apex Feeds reserves the operation and management of third-party marketplace sales channels for Apex Feeds itself. A Retailer may only sell Apex Feeds products through a third-party marketplace where Apex Feeds has provided specific prior written authorisation.</p>
<p>Permission granted for one marketplace, account or particular arrangement does not constitute permission to sell through any other marketplace or third-party platform.</p>
<p>For clarity, advertising or selling products through the Retailer’s own official Facebook or Instagram business presence under Section 8.3 is not considered third-party marketplace selling merely because the social-media service is operated by a third party.</p>
<p>However, listing products through Facebook Marketplace or an equivalent marketplace function is not permitted without written approval.</p>
<h4 id="s8-5">8.5 Resupply and Wholesale Redistribution</h4>
<p>Products purchased under an Apex Feeds wholesale account are supplied for resale to end consumers through the Retailer’s authorised sales channels. The Retailer must not use its Apex Feeds wholesale account to operate as an unauthorised wholesaler, distributor or supplier of Apex Feeds products to other retailers or resellers.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds products must not be supplied for commercial resale to another:</p>
<ul>
<li>pet store;</li>
<li>retailer;</li>
<li>online seller;</li>
<li>wholesaler;</li>
<li>distributor;</li>
<li>breeder or commercial operator intending to resell the products; or</li>
<li>other third-party reseller, unless Apex Feeds has provided prior written authorisation.</li>
</ul>
<p>Businesses wishing to commercially resell Apex Feeds products must apply for their own wholesale account or other appropriate commercial arrangement with Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s8-6">8.6 Bulk Purchases by End Consumers</h4>
<p>Nothing in Section 8.5 prevents a Retailer from selling larger quantities of Apex Feeds products to legitimate end consumers. This may include reptile keepers, breeders, wildlife carers, zoological facilities or other customers purchasing products for use in feeding or caring for animals under their control.</p>
<p>A bulk purchase does not constitute unauthorised redistribution merely because of the quantity purchased.</p>
<p>However, where the Retailer knows or reasonably believes that products are being purchased for onward commercial resale, the Retailer must not knowingly use its wholesale account to facilitate unauthorised redistribution of Apex Feeds products.</p>
<h4 id="s8-7">8.7 Expos, Shows and Temporary Retail Events</h4>
<p>Authorised Retailers may advertise and sell Apex Feeds products at reptile expos, pet shows, trade shows, exhibitions, temporary retail stalls and similar events where the Retailer is participating under its own approved business identity.</p>
<p>Separate Apex Feeds approval is not ordinarily required for each event. Products sold or displayed at these events remain subject to all applicable Apex Feeds requirements concerning:</p>
<ul>
<li>storage;</li>
<li>temperature control;</li>
<li>product handling;</li>
<li>hygiene;</li>
<li>presentation;</li>
<li>advertising;</li>
<li>product claims; and</li>
<li>sale of products within their applicable shelf life.</li>
</ul>
<p>Participation at an event does not authorise the Retailer to wholesale or redistribute Apex Feeds products to other participating businesses.</p>
<h4 id="s8-8">8.8 Australian Online Sales</h4>
<p>Authorised Retailers may sell eligible Apex Feeds products through their own authorised website to customers throughout Australia. The Retailer is responsible for determining whether a particular product can lawfully and appropriately be supplied to the customer’s destination.</p>
<p>This is particularly relevant to live feeder insects, biological products or other goods that may be subject to state or territory restrictions, biosecurity requirements or other controls.</p>
<p>Authorised Retailer status does not override any applicable Commonwealth, state or territory law or restriction.</p>
<h4 id="s8-9">8.9 International Sales and Export</h4>
<p>Wholesale approval is intended for the Australian retail market. The Retailer must not commercially export, distribute or sell Apex Feeds products to customers outside Australia without prior written approval from Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Any approved international distribution or export arrangement may be subject to separate terms and requirements.</p>
<h4 id="s8-10">8.10 Dropshipping and Direct-to-Customer Fulfilment</h4>
<p>Wholesale approval does not require Apex Feeds to provide dropshipping, fulfilment or direct-to-consumer delivery services on behalf of the Retailer. The Retailer is ordinarily responsible for purchasing, receiving, storing and fulfilling products sold through its authorised retail channels.</p>
<p>Any arrangement under which Apex Feeds dispatches products directly to customers on behalf of a Retailer must be separately agreed in writing and may be subject to additional fees, procedures and commercial terms.</p>
<h4 id="s8-11">8.11 Sale Through Unauthorised Businesses or Premises</h4>
<p>The Retailer must not use its wholesale account to establish Apex Feeds stock for ongoing retail sale through an unrelated or unauthorised business. This includes consignment, shelf-rental or similar arrangements designed to make Apex Feeds products available for retail sale through another business that has not been approved by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Where another business wishes to stock and resell Apex Feeds products, that business must obtain its own approval from Apex Feeds unless another arrangement has been expressly authorised in writing.</p>
<h4 id="s8-12">8.12 Original Packaging and Product Integrity</h4>
<p>Unless specifically authorised in writing by Apex Feeds, products must be resold in their original Apex Feeds retail packaging.</p>
<p>The Retailer must not:</p>
<ul>
<li>divide bulk Apex Feeds products into smaller retail quantities;</li>
<li>remove or obscure required product labels;</li>
<li>replace Apex Feeds product labels with retailer-branded labels;</li>
<li>represent repackaged products as original Apex Feeds retail products;</li>
<li>alter batch, best-before or traceability information; or</li>
<li>manufacture or create another product using Apex Feeds products and represent that resulting product as an Apex Feeds product.</li>
</ul>
<p>This does not prevent unopened Apex Feeds products from being included within legitimate retail bundles, starter packs, gift packs or similar promotions provided the individual Apex Feeds product remains in its original packaging and is accurately represented.</p>
<h3 id="s9">9. Unauthorised Resupply, Diversion &amp; Product Traceability</h3>
<p>Apex Feeds supplies wholesale products to Authorised Retailers for resale to end consumers through the authorised sales channels established under this Agreement. Wholesale approval does not appoint the</p>
<p>Retailer as a wholesaler, distributor or commercial supplier of Apex Feeds products to other businesses. The Retailer must take reasonable steps to ensure products purchased through its wholesale account are not knowingly diverted into unauthorised commercial resale channels.</p>
<h4 id="s9-1">9.1 Resale to End Consumers</h4>
<p>Products purchased through an Apex Feeds wholesale account are intended for resale to end consumers through the Retailer’s authorised physical stores, website, social-media presence, events and other sales channels permitted under Section 8.</p>
<p>An end consumer may include an individual keeper, breeder, wildlife carer, zoological facility, animal-care organisation or other customer purchasing Apex Feeds products for use rather than onward commercial resale. The quantity purchased by a customer does not, by itself, determine whether that customer is an end consumer.</p>
<h4 id="s9-2">9.2 Unauthorised Commercial Resupply</h4>
<p>Unless Apex Feeds has provided prior written approval, the Retailer must not knowingly purchase, supply, transfer or otherwise make Apex Feeds products available to another business for the purpose of onward commercial resale. This includes supplying products to another: * pet store or retail business; * online retailer; * wholesaler or distributor; * commercial reseller; * marketplace seller; or * other third party purchasing products for onward resale. Businesses wishing to commercially resell Apex Feeds products must establish their own approved wholesale account or other authorised commercial arrangement with Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s9-3">9.3 Transfers Between Locations of the Same Retailer</h4>
<p>A Retailer operating multiple locations under the same approved legal entity and ABN may transfer Apex Feeds stock between those locations for ordinary inventory management purposes.</p>
<p>Internal transfers do not constitute unauthorised resupply provided all receiving locations remain operated by the same approved legal entity and comply with the requirements of this Agreement. This permission does not extend to separately owned businesses, franchisees, licensees or businesses operating under a different legal entity or ABN.</p>
<h4 id="s9-4">9.4 Transfers Between Separate Authorised Retailers</h4>
<p>The fact that two businesses are independently approved Apex Feeds Retailers does not authorise them to commercially supply Apex Feeds products to one another.</p>
<p>Each Authorised Retailer is ordinarily required to purchase wholesale stock through its own Apex Feeds account. Where exceptional circumstances require stock to be transferred between separately owned Authorised Retailers, prior approval should be obtained from Apex Feeds. This allows Apex Feeds to maintain appropriate wholesale account, invoicing and product traceability records.</p>
<h4 id="s9-5">9.5 Suspected Product Diversion</h4>
<p>Where Apex Feeds has reasonable grounds to believe that products supplied to a Retailer are being diverted into unauthorised resale or distribution channels, Apex Feeds may request information reasonably necessary to investigate the concern.</p>
<p>Such information may include:</p>
<ul>
<li>relevant product and quantity information;</li>
<li>the locations at which affected stock is being sold;</li>
<li>information concerning unusual or significant wholesale quantities;</li>
<li>confirmation of whether products have been supplied to another business; and</li>
<li>other information reasonably connected with the suspected diversion.</li>
</ul>
<p>Apex Feeds will not require disclosure of the Retailer’s entire customer database or unrelated confidential customer information where that information is not reasonably necessary for the investigation. While a genuine diversion concern is being investigated, Apex Feeds may temporarily restrict further supply of the affected products where reasonably necessary to prevent continued unauthorised distribution.</p>
<h4 id="s9-6">9.6 Deliberate or Repeated Unauthorised Resupply</h4>
<p>Where unauthorised resupply appears to have resulted from a genuine misunderstanding or isolated error, Apex Feeds may require the Retailer to cease the activity and take reasonable corrective action.</p>
<p>Knowingly or deliberately supplying Apex Feeds products for unauthorised commercial resale, continuing such activity after being directed to cease, or repeatedly diverting products into unauthorised distribution channels may constitute a significant breach of this Agreement.</p>
<p>Any suspension or termination arising from such conduct will be dealt with in accordance with the applicable Breach, Corrective Action, Suspension and Termination provisions of this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s9-7">9.7 Product Batch and Traceability Information</h4>
<p>The Retailer must preserve batch numbers, best-before information, product identification and other traceability information applied to Apex Feeds products. The Retailer must not intentionally remove, alter, obscure, replace or falsify product traceability information.</p>
<p>Retailers are not ordinarily required to record the batch number of every individual product sold to every end consumer unless required by law or specifically required as part of an agreed traceability program. However, Retailers must reasonably cooperate with Apex Feeds where information is required to investigate a specific product, batch, quality concern, withdrawal or recall.</p>
<h4 id="s9-8">9.8 Traceability Enquiries</h4>
<p>Where Apex Feeds identifies a potential concern affecting a particular product or production batch, the Retailer may be requested to provide reasonable information concerning:</p>
<ul>
<li>whether affected stock remains in the Retailer’s possession;</li>
<li>quantities of affected stock currently held;</li>
<li>authorised locations holding the affected stock;</li>
<li>whether affected products have already been sold;</li>
<li>approximate quantities sold where reasonably ascertainable; and</li>
<li>other information reasonably required to identify and control affected products.</li>
</ul>
<p>The level of information requested will be proportionate to the nature and seriousness of the issue being investigated.</p>
<h4 id="s9-9">9.9 Product Quarantine</h4>
<p>Where Apex Feeds reasonably identifies a potential safety, quality, contamination, manufacturing or regulatory concern affecting particular stock, Apex Feeds may instruct the Retailer to temporarily remove identified products from sale and quarantine the affected stock while the matter is investigated.</p>
<p>The Retailer must take reasonable steps to ensure quarantined products are clearly separated or otherwise controlled so that they are not inadvertently sold, used or transferred. A quarantine instruction does not necessarily mean that the affected product has been determined to be defective or unsafe.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds will provide further instructions once sufficient information is available to determine the appropriate action.</p>
<h4 id="s9-10">9.10 Product Withdrawal and Recall Cooperation</h4>
<p>Where Apex Feeds initiates a product withdrawal or recall, the Retailer must promptly cooperate with reasonable instructions issued by Apex Feeds concerning the affected products.</p>
<p>This may include instructions to:</p>
<ul>
<li>immediately cease sale of identified products;</li>
<li>remove affected stock from shelves, websites and other sales channels;</li>
<li>quarantine remaining stock;</li>
<li>identify quantities remaining in the Retailer’s possession;</li>
<li>provide relevant batch or inventory information;</li>
<li>display or communicate customer information where reasonably required;</li>
<li>return, hold or dispose of affected products as instructed; and</li>
<li>assist with other reasonable measures necessary to implement the withdrawal or recall.</li>
</ul>
<p>Detailed procedures concerning product withdrawals and recalls are contained within Section 27 — Product Withdrawal &amp; Recall and any applicable Schedule.</p>
<h4 id="s9-11">9.11 Preservation of Affected Stock</h4>
<p>Where a product is subject to a quality investigation, traceability enquiry, withdrawal or recall, the Retailer must not knowingly dispose of, destroy, relabel, repurpose or otherwise alter the affected stock unless:</p>
<ul>
<li>Apex Feeds has authorised the action;</li>
<li>immediate disposal is reasonably necessary for safety reasons; or</li>
<li>disposal is required by law or a relevant authority.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where immediate disposal is necessary, the Retailer should, where reasonably practicable, retain photographs, batch information and other evidence sufficient to identify the affected products.</p>
<h4 id="s9-12">9.12 Cooperation and Record Integrity</h4>
<p>The Retailer must provide information requested under this Section honestly and must not knowingly conceal, alter or falsify information relating to the source, location, quantity, batch identity or onward commercial supply of Apex Feeds products. Nothing in this Section requires the Retailer to provide information unrelated to a legitimate product traceability, distribution, quality, safety or compliance matter.</p>
<h2 id="part-c">Part C: Brand Standards</h2>
<h3 id="s10">10. Apex Feeds Brand &amp; Intellectual Property</h3>
<p>Apex Feeds owns or controls the intellectual property and brand assets created for and used in connection with the Apex Feeds business and its products. Authorised Retailers are encouraged to actively promote Apex Feeds products through their stores, websites and approved social-media channels.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds grants Authorised Retailers limited permission to use approved Apex Feeds brand and marketing materials for the legitimate advertising, promotion and resale of genuine Apex Feeds products in accordance with this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s10-1">10.1 Apex Feeds Brand Assets</h4>
<p>For the purposes of this Agreement, Apex Feeds brand and marketing assets may include:</p>
<ul>
<li>the Apex Feeds business and brand name;</li>
<li>Apex Feeds logos and graphic elements;</li>
<li>the “Nutrition You Can See” slogan;</li>
<li>packaging and label artwork;</li>
<li>Apex-created product photography;</li>
<li>graphics and promotional artwork;</li>
<li>brochures, posters and point-of-sale materials;</li>
<li>Apex-created written product descriptions and advertising copy;</li>
<li>website and social-media marketing material; and</li>
<li>other original advertising, creative or brand material supplied by Apex Feeds for retailer use.</li>
</ul>
<p>Nothing in this Agreement transfers ownership of Apex Feeds intellectual property or brand assets to the Retailer.</p>
<h4 id="s10-2">10.2 Retailer Permission to Use</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds Materials While participating in the Apex Feeds wholesale program, the Retailer may use Apex Feeds marketing and brand materials made available for retailer use for the purpose of advertising, promoting and selling genuine Apex Feeds products.</p>
<p>This permission includes reasonable use across the Retailer’s:</p>
<ul>
<li>physical store;</li>
<li>own website;</li>
<li>Facebook and Instagram business accounts;</li>
<li>other authorised social-media channels;</li>
<li>catalogues and promotional material;</li>
<li>in-store displays; and</li>
<li>authorised expos, shows and temporary retail events.</li>
</ul>
<p>Separate approval is not required each time an Authorised Retailer uses material that Apex Feeds has provided or made available for retailer advertising. Use remains subject to this Agreement and any applicable Brand Standards.</p>
<h4 id="s10-3">10.3 Apex Feeds Logos</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds logos must be reproduced accurately and must not be modified without prior written approval from Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Retailers must not:</p>
<ul>
<li>alter the proportions or individual elements of a logo;</li>
<li>change its wording; * redraw or recreate the logo;</li>
<li>remove elements from it;</li>
<li>add elements that form part of the logo itself;</li>
<li>distort, rotate or otherwise materially modify it; or</li>
<li>create a modified or derivative Apex Feeds logo.</li>
</ul>
<p>Reasonable proportional resizing for different advertising formats is permitted. Detailed logo specifications may be provided through Apex Feeds Brand Standards or approved marketing resources.</p>
<h4 id="s10-4">10.4 Apex-Created Artwork and Advertising Materials</h4>
<p>Retailers may incorporate Apex Feeds supplied artwork, product photographs and advertising materials into their own advertisements. For example, a Retailer may combine an Apex Feeds product image with its own store branding, retail price, contact information or promotional message. However, the underlying Apex Feeds artwork must not be materially modified in a way that alters Apex Feeds branding, product information, imagery or claims without prior approval.</p>
<p>The Retailer must not modify Apex Feeds material in a manner that creates a false, inaccurate or misleading representation of Apex Feeds or its products.</p>
<h4 id="s10-5">10.5 Retailer-Created Advertising</h4>
<p>Retailers are encouraged to create their own advertising and promotional content featuring genuine Apex Feeds products. This may include photographs, videos, social-media posts, reels, product displays and other original content created within or for the Retailer’s business.</p>
<p>Retailer-created advertising must accurately represent the Apex Feeds products shown and comply with the applicable advertising, product representation and Brand Standards contained within this Agreement. Retailer-created advertising does not become the property of Apex Feeds merely because it contains or depicts an Apex Feeds product, logo or other permitted brand material.</p>
<h4 id="s10-6">10.6 Ownership and Use of Retailer-Created Content</h4>
<p>Original photographs, videos and other creative material independently produced by or for the Retailer remain the property of their respective owner, subject to any rights contained in the Apex Feeds material appearing within that content. Apex Feeds does not obtain ownership of retailer-created content merely because the content promotes Apex Feeds products.</p>
<p>Where Apex Feeds wishes to separately reproduce retailer-created photographs, videos or other original content within Apex Feeds advertising or marketing material, Apex Feeds will obtain appropriate permission from the Retailer or relevant rights holder. Nothing in this clause prevents Apex Feeds from using ordinary social-media functionality to share, repost or otherwise amplify a Retailer’s public post in a manner supported by the applicable platform.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may identify and promote the Retailer when sharing such content.</p>
<h4 id="s10-7">10.7 Misrepresentation of Association</h4>
<p>The Retailer must not represent itself as:</p>
<ul>
<li>Apex Feeds itself;</li>
<li>an employee or agent of Apex Feeds;</li>
<li>an exclusive distributor of Apex Feeds;</li>
<li>the manufacturer of Apex Feeds products;</li>
<li>an Apex Feeds-owned store; or</li>
<li>otherwise having an affiliation or authority beyond its actual Authorised Retailer relationship.</li>
</ul>
<p>While its Authorised Retailer status remains current, the Retailer may accurately describe itself as an “Authorised Apex Feeds Retailer” or use another description approved by Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s10-8">10.8 Business Names, Domains and Social-Media Identities</h4>
<p>Authorised Retailer status does not permit the Retailer to register or operate a business name, trading name, domain name, social-media account or similar commercial identity that falsely suggests it is Apex Feeds or an official Apex Feeds-operated business.</p>
<p>Without prior written approval, the Retailer must not establish accounts, domains or business identities using the Apex Feeds name in a manner reasonably likely to cause customers to believe the account, website or business is owned or operated by Apex Feeds. This does not prevent a Retailer from accurately advertising that it stocks, sells or is an Authorised Retailer of Apex Feeds products.</p>
<h4 id="s10-9">10.9 Unauthorised Products and Brand Use</h4>
<p>The Retailer must not apply Apex Feeds branding, labels, logos or packaging to a product that has not been manufactured, supplied or authorised by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>The Retailer must not:</p>
<ul>
<li>manufacture a product and represent it as an Apex Feeds product;</li>
<li>apply Apex Feeds labels or branding to another manufacturer’s product;</li>
<li>create an unauthorised co-branded product;</li>
<li>represent another product as being manufactured or endorsed by Apex Feeds where it is not; or</li>
<li>otherwise use Apex Feeds branding to create a false impression regarding the origin or endorsement of a product.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id="s10-10">10.10 Advertising Apex Feeds Online</h4>
<p>Retailers may use Apex Feeds branding and product names to truthfully advertise that they stock and sell Apex Feeds products through the authorised channels established under Section 8. Online advertising must clearly identify the Retailer where necessary to avoid creating a misleading impression that the advertisement, website, page or account is operated directly by Apex Feeds. Nothing in this Section authorises sales through third-party marketplaces prohibited under Section 8.</p>
<h4 id="s10-11">10.11 Cessation of Authorised Retailer Status</h4>
<p>When a Retailer’s Authorised Retailer status ends, the Retailer must cease representing itself as a current Authorised Apex Feeds Retailer. Where the Retailer legitimately retains genuine Apex Feeds stock that it previously purchased, it may continue to use Apex Feeds product information, photographs and other reasonably necessary marketing materials for the limited purpose of identifying, advertising and selling that remaining genuine stock.</p>
<p>This includes circumstances involving business closure, liquidation, store closure or clearance of remaining inventory. The Retailer is not required to dispose of genuine Apex Feeds stock solely because its Authorised Retailer relationship has ended.</p>
<p>Any continuing use of Apex Feeds material must accurately relate to genuine remaining Apex Feeds stock and must not create the impression that the Retailer’s wholesale account or Authorised Retailer status remains active. Once the Retailer’s remaining Apex Feeds inventory has been sold or otherwise disposed of, continued commercial use of Apex Feeds marketing materials must cease unless separately authorised.</p>
<h3 id="s11">11. Advertising &amp; Social Media</h3>
<p>Apex Feeds encourages Authorised Retailers to actively advertise, promote and educate customers about Apex Feeds products through their approved retail channels. Retailers are encouraged to create engaging, informative and original content that supports their own business while accurately representing Apex Feeds products and maintaining the professional reputation of both Apex Feeds and the Retailer.</p>
<p>Retailers do not require prior approval from Apex Feeds for ordinary advertising that complies with this Agreement and the applicable Brand Standards.</p>
<h4 id="s11-1">11.1 Permitted Advertising</h4>
<p>Authorised Retailers may advertise and promote Apex Feeds products through the sales and marketing channels permitted under Section 8, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>the Retailer’s physical stores;</li>
<li>the Retailer’s own website;</li>
<li>official Facebook and Instagram business accounts;</li>
<li>other authorised business social-media accounts;</li>
<li>email marketing;</li>
<li>catalogues and flyers;</li>
<li>in-store signage and displays;</li>
<li>paid digital advertising; and</li>
<li>authorised expos, shows and temporary retail events.</li>
</ul>
<p>Advertising through a permitted channel remains subject to the requirements of this Agreement regardless of the format or platform used.</p>
<h4 id="s11-2">11.2 Apex Feeds Advertising Materials</h4>
<p>Retailers may use product photographs, graphics, written product information, promotional material and other advertising resources supplied or made available by Apex Feeds for Authorised Retailer use.</p>
<p>Retailers are encouraged to use these materials where appropriate to maintain accurate and consistent product representation.</p>
<p>Use and modification of Apex Feeds logos, artwork and other intellectual property remains subject to Section 10 and the applicable Brand Standards.</p>
<h4 id="s11-3">11.3 Retailer-Created Content</h4>
<p>Retailers are encouraged to produce their own original advertising content featuring genuine Apex Feeds products.</p>
<p>This may include:</p>
<ul>
<li>photographs;</li>
<li>videos and reels;</li>
<li>product demonstrations;</li>
<li>feeding demonstrations;</li>
<li>new-stock announcements;</li>
<li>educational content;</li>
<li>store displays;</li>
<li>staff recommendations; and</li>
<li>other genuine promotional content relevant to the Retailer’s business.</li>
</ul>
<p>Retailer-created content must accurately represent the products shown and must not contain false, misleading or unsubstantiated representations concerning Apex Feeds or its products.</p>
<h4 id="s11-4">11.4 Retailer Responsibility for Advertising</h4>
<p>The Retailer is responsible for advertising published through or on behalf of its business. This responsibility includes advertising created or prepared by employees, contractors, marketing agencies, influencers, content creators or other persons engaged by the Retailer. The Retailer must take reasonable steps to ensure advertising published through its business complies with this Agreement, applicable Brand Standards and relevant advertising and consumer laws.</p>
<h4 id="s11-5">11.5 Store-Specific Discounts and Promotions</h4>
<p>Retailers may independently establish and advertise their own retail discounts, sales, clearance offers, multi-buy offers and other promotions involving Apex Feeds products. Where a promotion has been independently established by the Retailer, advertising must clearly present the promotion as an offer of the Retailer’s own business and must not create the impression that it is an Apex Feeds promotion, national campaign or manufacturer-funded offer.</p>
<p>For example, a Retailer may advertise: “John’s Pets — 20% off Apex Feeds this weekend.” The Retailer must not represent the promotion as an “Apex Feeds Sale”, “Apex Feeds National Promotion” or similar Apex-operated campaign unless Apex Feeds has actually authorised or conducted that promotion.</p>
<p>Nothing in this clause restricts the Retailer’s independent determination of its retail prices in accordance with Section 6.</p>
<h4 id="s11-6">11.6 Apex Feeds Promotions</h4>
<p>Where Apex Feeds conducts an official promotion and makes promotional material available to participating Retailers, Retailers may advertise that promotion in accordance with its stated conditions. Retailers must accurately represent the applicable dates, products, offers and other conditions of an Apex Feeds promotion.</p>
<p>A Retailer must not continue advertising an expired Apex Feeds promotion or materially alter its terms in a manner that misleads customers.</p>
<h4 id="s11-7">11.7 Product and Brand Comparisons</h4>
<p>Retailers may make genuine comparisons between Apex Feeds products and competing products or brands provided those comparisons are fair, accurate and not misleading or deceptive. Where a comparison is presented as factual, the Retailer must have a reasonable basis for the representation being made.</p>
<p>Retailers may express genuine opinions regarding products they stock or recommend. However, Apex Feeds branding must not be used to publish material whose primary purpose is to unfairly disparage, ridicule or damage the reputation of another manufacturer, retailer or competing business.</p>
<p>Comparative advertising should focus on legitimate product characteristics, differences and customer information rather than personal attacks or unnecessary denigration of another business. Unless specifically authorised, a Retailer’s comparative statement must not be presented as an official statement or position of Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s11-8">11.8 Giveaways, Competitions and Prizes</h4>
<p>Authorised Retailers may independently use genuine Apex Feeds products lawfully purchased by the Retailer as prizes in giveaways, competitions, customer promotions or similar activities. Separate approval from Apex Feeds is not ordinarily required.</p>
<p>Where Apex Feeds has not sponsored or participated in the promotion, the Retailer must not represent or imply that:</p>
<ul>
<li>Apex Feeds is conducting the competition;</li>
<li>Apex Feeds is an official sponsor;</li>
<li>Apex Feeds has endorsed the competition; or</li>
<li>the promotion is an official Apex Feeds campaign.</li>
</ul>
<p>The Retailer remains responsible for conducting its promotion in accordance with applicable laws and platform requirements.</p>
<h4 id="s11-9">11.9 Influencers and Content Creators</h4>
<p>Authorised Retailers may engage influencers, ambassadors, content creators, photographers or other third parties to assist in creating promotional content involving Apex Feeds products. Where such content is created for the Retailer, the Retailer must review and publish or otherwise authorise the content through its own business channels and remains responsible for ensuring that the resulting advertising complies with this Agreement.</p>
<p>The Retailer must take reasonable steps to ensure that content created on its behalf maintains the professional presentation and reputation of both the Retailer’s business and the Apex Feeds brand.</p>
<p>A Retailer must not appoint, describe or present an influencer, content creator or other person as an official Apex Feeds ambassador, representative, sponsored athlete, spokesperson or agent without prior written approval from Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s11-10">11.10 Social-Media Tagging and Community Promotion</h4>
<p>Retailers are encouraged to tag or identify Apex Feeds in genuine social-media content featuring Apex Feeds products. Apex Feeds may use ordinary platform sharing and reposting functionality to amplify public retailer content and may identify or promote the originating Authorised Retailer when doing so, consistent with Section 10.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds recognises that retailer participation, customer engagement and community-generated content can contribute positively to the development of both the Apex Feeds brand and its Authorised Retailer network.</p>
<h4 id="s11-11">11.11 Customer Questions and Complaints on Social Media</h4>
<p>Retailers should respond professionally to genuine customer questions, concerns or complaints concerning Apex Feeds products. Retailers are not required or expected to suppress legitimate negative feedback or customer complaints.</p>
<p>Where a complaint involves a potential manufacturing defect, contamination, spoilage, animal-safety concern or other significant product-quality issue, the Retailer should direct or escalate the matter through the applicable Apex Feeds product claims procedure.</p>
<p>Where the cause of an issue has not been established, the Retailer should avoid presenting speculation regarding responsibility as established fact. Nothing in this clause prevents a Retailer from providing customers with accurate information concerning a genuine issue or exercising any obligation imposed by law.</p>
<h4 id="s11-12">11.12 False Association or Endorsement</h4>
<p>Advertising must not create a false or misleading impression that: * the Retailer is owned or operated by Apex Feeds;</p>
<ul>
<li>Apex Feeds created or approved retailer-generated advertising where it did not;</li>
<li>Apex Feeds sponsors an individual, organisation, event or promotion where it does not;</li>
<li>a Retailer-created campaign is an official Apex Feeds campaign; or</li>
<li>the Retailer has authority to make statements or commitments on behalf of Apex Feeds.</li>
</ul>
<p>Retailers may accurately represent themselves as an Authorised Apex Feeds Retailer while that status remains current.</p>
<h4 id="s11-13">11.13 Advertising Compliance</h4>
<p>Where Apex Feeds reasonably identifies retailer advertising that contains materially inaccurate product information, unauthorised Apex Feeds claims, modified Apex Feeds artwork, false association or other material non-compliance with this Agreement, Apex Feeds may request that the Retailer correct or remove the affected material within a reasonable period.</p>
<p>Where the issue presents an immediate product-safety, legal or serious reputational concern, Apex Feeds may request that the affected material be removed or corrected promptly while the matter is reviewed. Minor differences in retailer advertising style, opinion, photography or presentation will not, by themselves, constitute a breach merely because Apex Feeds would have advertised the product differently.</p>
<h3 id="s12">12. Product Claims &amp; Representation</h3>
<p>Apex Feeds provides detailed product information to assist Authorised Retailers in accurately explaining, recommending and promoting Apex Feeds products to customers. This information may include product labels, long-form product descriptions, website information, ingredient information, nutritional information, feeding and preparation instructions, product literature and other materials supplied by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Retailers are encouraged to use this information when educating customers and advertising Apex Feeds products. The Retailer may explain Apex Feeds product information in its own words provided the meaning remains accurate and the Retailer does not materially exaggerate, alter or misrepresent the information supplied by Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s12-1">12.1 Approved Product Information</h4>
<p>For the purposes of representing Apex Feeds products, Retailers may rely upon current information provided by Apex Feeds through:</p>
<ul>
<li>product packaging and labels;</li>
<li>official Apex Feeds website product descriptions;</li>
<li>long-form product descriptions;</li>
<li>ingredient and nutritional information;</li>
<li>feeding and preparation instructions;</li>
<li>retailer product information;</li>
<li>catalogues and brochures;</li>
<li>official Apex Feeds social-media or promotional material; and</li>
<li>other written product information supplied by Apex Feeds.</li>
</ul>
<p>Retailers are not required to reproduce this information word-for-word and may reasonably adapt it for customer conversations, advertising and their own store format provided the substance of the information remains accurate.</p>
<h4 id="s12-2">12.2 Long-Form Product Descriptions</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds long-form product descriptions are specifically intended to provide Retailers and customers with more detailed information concerning the purpose, formulation, ingredients, preparation, feeding application and distinguishing characteristics of individual products and product ranges.</p>
<p>Authorised Retailers may use, reproduce, summarise or draw upon these descriptions when: * creating website product listings;</p>
<ul>
<li>educating customers;</li>
<li>training staff;</li>
<li>producing social-media content;</li>
<li>creating store advertising;</li>
<li>answering customer questions; and</li>
<li>comparing products within the Apex Feeds range.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where a Retailer summarises or rewrites Apex Feeds product information, it must take reasonable care not to change its material meaning or create claims beyond those contained in or reasonably supported by the source information.</p>
<h4 id="s12-3">12.3 Retailer Knowledge and Husbandry Advice</h4>
<p>Nothing in this Agreement prevents Retailers or their staff from using their own knowledge, professional experience or practical husbandry experience when advising customers. Retailers and their staff may provide independent advice concerning animal husbandry, feeding practices, product selection and their personal experience using Apex Feeds products.</p>
<p>Where advice materially differs from official Apex Feeds instructions or recommendations, the Retailer should not represent that advice as an official recommendation or instruction of Apex Feeds. Personal experience should be represented as such and must not be converted into a guaranteed product outcome or false factual claim.</p>
<h4 id="s12-4">12.4 Product Ingredients and Composition</h4>
<p>Where a Retailer makes factual representations regarding the ingredients, composition or nutritional characteristics of an Apex Feeds product, those representations must be based on information applicable to the relevant product.</p>
<p>Retailers should take reasonable steps to use current Apex Feeds information, particularly where product formulations, ingredients, packaging or nutritional information have been updated.</p>
<p>Where information from an older advertisement, webpage or promotional resource conflicts with information applicable to the product or batch actually being sold, the Retailer should rely upon the information applicable to the product being supplied and contact Apex Feeds where clarification is required.</p>
<h4 id="s12-5">12.5 Feeding and Preparation Instructions</h4>
<p>Retailers may explain and demonstrate Apex Feeds preparation and feeding instructions to customers. Where a preparation method, mixing ratio, storage instruction or feeding direction is represented as an Apex Feeds instruction, it must remain materially consistent with the applicable information provided by Apex Feeds. Retailers may discuss their own practical methods or preferences provided these are not falsely represented as official Apex Feeds instructions and do not knowingly compromise product safety or integrity.</p>
<h4 id="s12-6">12.6 Species and Feeding Suitability</h4>
<p> Retailers may assist customers in selecting Apex Feeds products for appropriate animals and may provide independent husbandry advice based on their own knowledge and experience. Where a Retailer represents that Apex Feeds itself has formulated, designed or specifically recommends a product for a particular species, life stage or feeding application, that representation must be consistent with information supplied by Apex Feeds. The Retailer must not attribute a species-specific recommendation to Apex Feeds where Apex Feeds has not made that recommendation.</p>
<h4 id="s12-7">12.7 Nutritional Adequacy and Complete-Diet Claims</h4>
<p>Claims that an Apex Feeds product constitutes a complete diet, complete and balanced diet, sole diet or otherwise provides all nutritional requirements for a particular animal or species must only be attributed to Apex Feeds where Apex Feeds has expressly made or authorised that representation for the relevant product.</p>
<p>A Retailer must not independently convert general nutritional, ingredient or feeding information into a stronger nutritional-adequacy claim and attribute that claim to Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>This does not prevent Retailers from providing their own lawful and appropriately qualified husbandry advice concerning how they personally incorporate Apex Feeds products into an animal’s diet.</p>
<h4 id="s12-8">12.8 Animal Health and Therapeutic Claims</h4>
<p>Unless expressly supported and authorised by Apex Feeds and permitted by applicable law, the Retailer must not represent Apex Feeds products as diagnosing, treating, curing or preventing a disease, medical condition or other animal-health disorder.</p>
<p>Retailers must not independently attribute therapeutic, veterinary or medicinal properties to an Apex Feeds product merely because it contains a particular ingredient or nutrient. This does not prevent ordinary discussion of nutrition, ingredients, feeding, husbandry or the normal nutritional role of ingredients where the information is accurate and appropriately represented.</p>
<h4 id="s12-9">12.9 Guaranteed Outcomes</h4>
<p>The Retailer must not make or attribute to Apex Feeds guarantees concerning individual animal responses or outcomes that Apex Feeds has not expressly provided.</p>
<p>This includes unsupported guarantees concerning:</p>
<ul>
<li>growth rates;</li>
<li>weight gain or loss;</li>
<li>breeding performance;</li>
<li>appetite or feeding acceptance;</li>
<li>reproductive outcomes;</li>
<li>disease prevention;</li>
<li>recovery from illness or injury; or</li>
<li>other specific physiological or performance outcomes.</li>
</ul>
<p>Retailers may discuss genuine personal experiences and customer experiences provided those experiences are not misleadingly presented as guaranteed outcomes for other animals.</p>
<h4 id="s12-10">12.10 Customer Reviews and Testimonials</h4>
<p>Retailers may publish, share or display genuine customer reviews and testimonials concerning Apex Feeds products. Where a Retailer actively republishes, highlights or incorporates a customer testimonial into its own advertising, the Retailer is responsible for taking reasonable steps to ensure that the resulting advertisement is not misleading or deceptive.</p>
<p>A customer statement must not be deliberately used as a means of making a product claim that would otherwise be inappropriate or misleading if made directly by the Retailer. For example, a customer independently commenting on a social-media post does not automatically make the Retailer responsible for the customer’s statement.</p>
<p>However, selecting that statement and reproducing it within a retailer-created advertisement may amount to the Retailer adopting the claim for promotional purposes.</p>
<h4 id="s12-11">12.11 Comparison Between Apex Feeds Products</h4>
<p>Retailers are encouraged to explain differences between Apex Feeds product ranges and individual products where doing so assists customers in selecting an appropriate product. Comparisons should accurately reflect relevant differences in formulation, ingredients, preparation, intended application or other product characteristics. Retailers must not invent differences or benefits that are not reasonably supported by the applicable product information.</p>
<h4 id="s12-12">12.12 Labels and Mandatory Product Information</h4>
<p>The Retailer must not intentionally remove, obscure, replace or materially alter product information appearing on Apex Feeds packaging where doing so could prevent customers from accessing relevant:</p>
<ul>
<li>product identification;</li>
<li>ingredients;</li>
<li>nutritional information;</li>
<li>preparation or feeding instructions;</li>
<li>storage information;</li>
<li>warnings;</li>
<li>batch information;</li>
<li>best-before information; or</li>
<li>other required product information.</li>
</ul>
<p>Ordinary retail price labels, inventory labels or similar store identification may be applied provided they do not materially obscure important Apex Feeds product information.</p>
<h4 id="s12-13">12.13 Questions and Product Clarification</h4>
<p>Where a Retailer or staff member is uncertain about the ingredients, formulation, preparation, intended use, feeding application or other characteristics of an Apex Feeds product, the Retailer is encouraged to contact Apex Feeds for clarification rather than speculate or provide uncertain information as fact. Apex Feeds may provide updated or additional product information where necessary to assist Retailers in accurately representing its products.</p>
<h4 id="s12-14">12.14 Retailer Suggestions and Product Information Feedback</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds welcomes feedback from Authorised Retailers regarding its product descriptions, feeding information, educational material and other product information.</p>
<p>Where Retailer staff identify information that they believe should be added, clarified, corrected or expanded within official Apex Feeds product information, the suggestion may be submitted to Apex Feeds for consideration.</p>
<p>To maintain clear and consistent communication between Apex Feeds and its wholesale accounts, proposed changes or additions should be submitted through the registered wholesale account owner or an authorised representative of the Retailer.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds will consider reasonable suggestions but is not required to adopt a proposed change. Where Apex Feeds accepts a suggestion, Apex Feeds will determine the appropriate wording and method of incorporating the change into its official product information.</p>
<p>Any resulting update may be communicated through product descriptions, website information, labels, retailer resources or other appropriate Apex Feeds channels.</p>
<p>Retailer staff must not independently alter Apex Feeds-supplied product descriptions or represent a proposed change, addition or clarification as official Apex Feeds information before that change has been accepted by Apex Feeds. Nothing in this clause prevents Retailer staff from providing their own knowledge, experience or husbandry advice in accordance with Section 12.3.</p>
<h4 id="s12-15">12.15 Correction of Materially Inaccurate Claims</h4>
<p>Where Apex Feeds reasonably identifies a materially inaccurate, misleading or unauthorised factual claim concerning an Apex Feeds product in retailer-controlled advertising, Apex Feeds may request that the Retailer correct or remove the affected claim within a reasonable period.</p>
<p>Where the representation creates an immediate animal-safety, legal or significant product-integrity concern, Apex Feeds may request prompt correction or removal while the matter is reviewed.</p>
<p>A difference of opinion concerning ordinary husbandry practices, personal product preference or retailer experience will not, by itself, constitute a breach of this Section merely because Apex Feeds would provide different advice.</p>
<h3 id="s13">13. In-Store Presentation</h3>
<p>Authorised Retailers are encouraged to present Apex Feeds products in a professional manner that supports effective customer education, product visibility and the overall presentation of both the Retailer’s business and the Apex Feeds brand.</p>
<p>Except where necessary for product safety, storage, identification or compliance with this Agreement, Apex Feeds does not prescribe mandatory shelf positions, minimum display areas or exclusive merchandising arrangements. Retailers remain responsible for determining how Apex Feeds products are incorporated into their individual store layout.</p>
<h4 id="s13-1">13.1 General Product Presentation</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds products offered for sale should be presented in a clean, professional and saleable condition. Products must not knowingly be offered for sale where packaging damage, contamination, deterioration or another condition reasonably indicates that the integrity or safety of the product may have been compromised.</p>
<p>Detailed requirements concerning storage, temperature control, stock rotation and compromised products are contained in Sections 14–19 and Schedule A.</p>
<h4 id="s13-2">13.2 Retailer Merchandising</h4>
<p>Retailers may determine the location, shelf arrangement and general merchandising of Apex Feeds products within their stores. Apex Feeds does not require dedicated shelf space, exclusive displays or separation from competing brands unless a particular arrangement is reasonably necessary for product safety or regulatory compliance.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may provide recommended merchandising layouts, display concepts or presentation guidance to assist Retailers. Unless expressly identified as a product-safety or compliance requirement, such guidance is advisory rather than mandatory.</p>
<h4 id="s13-3">13.3 Apex Feeds-Supplied Display Materials</h4>
<p> Authorised Retailers may display point-of-sale and promotional materials supplied or approved by Apex Feeds, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>posters;</li>
<li>banners;</li>
<li>shelf talkers;</li>
<li>product information cards;</li>
<li>educational material;</li>
<li>counter displays;</li>
<li>product-range signage;</li>
<li>promotional graphics; and</li>
<li>other approved retail display materials.</li>
</ul>
<p>Retailers are encouraged to contact Apex Feeds where additional material is required to support an Apex Feeds display.</p>
<h4 id="s13-4">13.4 Custom Retailer-Created Displays and Signage</h4>
<p>Retailers are encouraged to develop custom displays, signage and merchandising concepts that suit the individual presentation and layout of their store. Where a custom display, sign, banner, wall graphic, fixture or other permanent or substantial promotional material incorporates the Apex Feeds name, logo, artwork or other Apex Feeds brand assets, the final design must be submitted to and approved by Apex Feeds before manufacture, printing or installation.</p>
<p>Approval is intended to ensure that Apex Feeds branding is represented accurately and that the final design is suitable for use alongside the Retailer’s own branding and store presentation. Approval must not be unreasonably withheld where the proposed material accurately represents Apex Feeds and complies with the Brand Standards.</p>
<h4 id="s13-5">13.5 Retailer’s Own Designer, Printer or Signwriter</h4>
<p>Retailers may engage their own designer, printer, signwriter, display manufacturer or other supplier to produce custom Apex Feeds retail material. Where Apex Feeds brand assets are required for an approved project, Apex Feeds may provide appropriate artwork or production files directly to the Retailer or its nominated supplier where reasonably necessary.</p>
<p>The Retailer remains responsible for ensuring that the final design is approved by Apex Feeds before production. Approval of a design does not make Apex Feeds responsible for the Retailer’s independent supplier, production costs, installation, workmanship or contractual arrangements unless Apex Feeds has separately agreed otherwise in writing.</p>
<h4 id="s13-6">13.6 Apex Feeds Design and Production Assistance</h4>
<p>Where requested, Apex Feeds may assist an Authorised Retailer with the development of custom in-store advertising, signage, displays or other promotional material. Apex Feeds may arrange for its own team members or nominated designers, printers, signwriters or other suppliers to assist with design, manufacture, printing and delivery directly to the Retailer’s store.</p>
<p>The proposed design must be approved by both Apex Feeds and the Retailer before final production. Any applicable design, printing, manufacturing, freight, installation or other costs must be agreed with the Retailer before those costs are incurred. Nothing in this clause requires a Retailer to use an Apex Feeds-nominated supplier where the Retailer prefers to arrange its own approved design and production.</p>
<h4 id="s13-7">13.7 Approval of Custom Designs</h4>
<p>Approval of a custom design applies to the design submitted and does not constitute general approval for materially altered versions of that design. Minor production adjustments that do not materially alter the approved appearance or Apex Feeds branding do not require a new approval.</p>
<p>Where a Retailer wishes to materially change an approved design, the revised final design should be submitted to Apex Feeds before production. Apex Feeds will endeavour to review custom designs within a reasonable period so that approval requirements do not unnecessarily delay Retailer projects.</p>
<h4 id="s13-8">13.8 Retail Price and Inventory Labels</h4>
<p>Retailers may apply ordinary price labels, barcodes, inventory labels or other reasonable store identification to Apex Feeds products. Such labels must not materially obscure product identification, ingredients, nutritional information, feeding or preparation instructions, warnings, batch information, best-before information or other important product information.</p>
<h4 id="s13-9">13.9 Clearance and Short-Dated Stock</h4>
<p>Retailers may independently discount or clear Apex Feeds products, including short-dated stock, provided the product remains suitable for lawful sale and any applicable best-before, batch or product information remains visible and unaltered. Any clearance or discount established independently by the Retailer must be represented as a Retailer promotion in accordance with Sections 6 and 11.</p>
<h4 id="s13-10">13.10 Damaged or Compromised Products</h4>
<p>Where packaging damage, contamination, temperature exposure or another condition creates reasonable concern regarding product integrity, the affected product should be removed from sale and handled in accordance with the applicable Product Handling and Claims provisions of this Agreement. A cosmetically imperfect outer package does not automatically make a product unsuitable for sale where the product itself remains sealed, safe and otherwise fit for sale.</p>
<h4 id="s13-11">13.11 Frozen and Temperature-Controlled Products</h4>
<p>Frozen and other temperature-controlled Apex Feeds products must remain under the applicable storage conditions regardless of merchandising or display considerations. Retailers may use signage, photographs, product cards, freezer graphics or other approved materials to promote products where the physical product cannot appropriately be displayed outside its required storage environment.</p>
<p>Detailed temperature and handling requirements are contained in the applicable Product Handling provisions and Schedule A.</p>
<h4 id="s13-12">13.12 Live Feeders</h4>
<p>Retailers may determine how live Apex Feeds feeders are displayed within their store provided applicable containment, welfare, environmental, biosecurity and legal requirements are maintained. Detailed requirements concerning live feeder storage and handling are addressed separately under Section 17 and Schedule A.</p>
<h2 id="part-d">Part D: Product Handling</h2>
<h3 id="s14">14. General Storage &amp; Handling Requirements</h3>
<p>Authorised Retailers are responsible for maintaining the condition, safety and integrity of Apex Feeds products while those products are under the Retailer’s possession or control. Following successful delivery, Apex Feeds products must be stored, handled, transported and displayed in a manner appropriate to the relevant product category and consistent with the product label, this Agreement, Schedule A and any additional written storage or handling instructions supplied by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>The requirements of this Section apply generally to all Apex Feeds products. Additional requirements applicable to shelf-stable products, frozen products and live feeders are contained in Sections 15–17.</p>
<h4 id="s14-1">14.1 Retailer Responsibility Following Delivery</h4>
<p>Following successful delivery of an order, the Retailer is responsible for maintaining appropriate storage and handling conditions for Apex Feeds products while those products remain under the Retailer’s possession or control.</p>
<p>Product deterioration, spoilage, contamination or damage caused by inappropriate storage or handling after successful delivery will not ordinarily constitute a manufacturing defect or freight claim against Apex Feeds. Nothing in this clause excludes any right or remedy that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
<h4 id="s14-2">14.2 Compliance with Storage and Handling Instructions</h4>
<p>Retailers must take reasonable steps to comply with applicable storage and handling requirements contained in:</p>
<ul>
<li>the product packaging or label;</li>
<li>this Agreement;</li>
<li>Schedule A — Product Storage &amp; Handling Standards;</li>
<li>written product information supplied by Apex Feeds; and</li>
<li>subsequent written safety, storage or handling instructions issued by Apex Feeds for the relevant product.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where Apex Feeds becomes aware of a product-specific storage or handling requirement that materially affects product safety or integrity, Apex Feeds may communicate updated instructions to affected Retailers.</p>
<h4 id="s14-3">14.3 General Storage Environment</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds products must be stored in an environment reasonably appropriate for animal food, feed and related products. Retailers must take reasonable precautions to protect products from:</p>
<ul>
<li>excessive heat;</li>
<li>direct sunlight where detrimental to the product;</li>
<li>excessive humidity or moisture;</li>
<li>water exposure;</li>
<li>pests and vermin;</li>
<li>dirt and other environmental contamination;</li>
<li>chemical contamination;</li>
<li>damaged or unsanitary storage areas; and</li>
<li>other conditions reasonably likely to compromise product quality, packaging or safety.</li>
</ul>
<p>Products must not knowingly be stored in conditions that are visibly unsanitary or otherwise unsuitable for the relevant product.</p>
<h4 id="s14-4">14.4 Chemicals and Sources of Contamination</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds food and feed products must be reasonably separated from chemicals and other potential sources of contamination.</p>
<p>This includes cleaning chemicals, pesticides, fuels, solvents, veterinary chemicals and other substances capable of leaking, spilling, transferring odour or otherwise contaminating the product.</p>
<p>This clause does not require a separate dedicated storage room where reasonable physical separation and appropriate storage practices adequately protect the products from contamination.</p>
<h4 id="s14-5">14.5 Opened Retail Products</h4>
<p>Where a Retailer opens a factory-sealed Apex Feeds product for demonstration, sampling, staff education, display or another store purpose, that product must not subsequently be represented or sold to a customer as a new, unopened or factory-sealed Apex Feeds retail product.</p>
<p>Opened product may continue to be used for appropriate demonstration, sampling, educational or internal purposes provided it has been stored and handled appropriately and remains suitable for its intended use.</p>
<p>Nothing in this clause permits the Retailer to commercially repackage Apex Feeds products for resale under separate packaging unless specifically authorised by Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s14-6">14.6 Retailer-Prepared Samples</h4>
<p>Authorised Retailers may use genuine Apex Feeds products purchased by the Retailer to prepare or provide samples to customers. Apex Feeds does not require separate approval for ordinary in-store sampling conducted by an Authorised Retailer.</p>
<p>The Retailer is responsible for ensuring that the preparation, handling, storage and distribution of retailer-prepared samples complies with all applicable Commonwealth, state or territory and local government requirements, including any applicable food/feed safety, hygiene, animal-feed, premises or council requirements.</p>
<p>Retailers must take reasonable precautions to ensure samples are prepared hygienically, appropriately stored and protected from contamination. Where appropriate, customers should be informed that the sample has been prepared or repackaged by the Retailer rather than supplied by Apex Feeds as an individually factory-packaged retail product.</p>
<p>The Retailer must not apply an Apex Feeds retail label, batch number or other representation to a retailer-prepared sample in a manner that falsely suggests Apex Feeds manufactured or individually packaged that sample.</p>
<h4 id="s14-7">14.7 Internal Transfers Between Approved Locations</h4>
<p>A Retailer operating multiple approved locations under the same legal entity and ABN may transfer Apex Feeds stock between those locations in accordance with Section 9. The Retailer remains responsible for maintaining appropriate storage, handling and transport conditions during the transfer. Products requiring temperature control, live-animal management or other specialised handling must remain under the applicable conditions throughout the transfer.</p>
<h4 id="s14-8">14.8 Storage or Equipment Failure</h4>
<p>Where an event may reasonably have compromised Apex Feeds stock, the affected products must be removed from normal sale and appropriately segregated or quarantined while their condition is assessed.</p>
<p>Examples may include:</p>
<ul>
<li>freezer or refrigeration failure;</li>
<li>flooding or significant water exposure;</li>
<li>excessive heat exposure;</li>
<li>pest infestation;</li>
<li>chemical spills;</li>
<li>contamination events;</li>
<li>significant packaging failure; or</li>
<li>another event reasonably capable of affecting product safety or integrity.</li>
</ul>
<p>Retailers must not knowingly return potentially compromised products to sale merely because the products appear visually unaffected where there remains a reasonable safety or integrity concern. Where appropriate, the Retailer should contact Apex Feeds for guidance.</p>
<h4 id="s14-9">14.9 Quarantined Stock</h4>
<p>Quarantining a product does not, by itself, establish that the product is defective or unsuitable for sale. Quarantine is a precautionary measure intended to prevent potentially affected stock from being supplied to customers while the circumstances are assessed.</p>
<p>Affected products should remain identifiable and, where relevant, associated batch, best-before and quantity information should be retained until the matter is resolved.</p>
<h4 id="s14-10">14.10 Storage and Handling Investigations</h4>
<p>Where Apex Feeds has reasonable grounds to believe that Apex Feeds products may be stored or handled in a manner that materially compromises product safety, integrity or applicable storage requirements, Apex Feeds may request reasonable information from the Retailer to assist in assessing the concern.</p>
<p>Depending upon the circumstances, this may include relevant:</p>
<ul>
<li>photographs;</li>
<li>storage information;</li>
<li>temperature information where applicable;</li>
<li>product and batch information;</li>
<li>details of the affected stock;</li>
<li>information concerning a storage or equipment failure; or</li>
<li>other information reasonably related to the identified concern.</li>
</ul>
<p>Any request should be proportionate to the nature and seriousness of the issue being investigated.</p>
<h4 id="s14-11">14.11 Inspection of Relevant Storage Areas</h4>
<p> Where a genuine product-safety or integrity concern cannot reasonably be resolved through information provided by the Retailer, Apex Feeds may request an agreed inspection of the storage, display or handling area directly relevant to the affected Apex Feeds products.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds does not have an unrestricted right under this Agreement to inspect unrelated areas of the Retailer’s premises or business records. Any inspection should occur at a mutually reasonable time and be limited to what is reasonably necessary to investigate or resolve the identified concern, except where more immediate action is reasonably necessary because of an urgent product-safety issue.</p>
<h4 id="s14-12">14.12 Temporary Supply Restriction</h4>
<p>Where Apex Feeds has reasonable grounds to believe that continued supply of a particular product or product category may create a material product-safety or integrity risk because appropriate storage or handling conditions cannot presently be demonstrated, Apex Feeds may temporarily restrict supply of the affected product or category while the concern is investigated.</p>
<p>Any restriction should, where reasonably practicable, be limited to the affected product category rather than the Retailer’s entire wholesale account. Supply may resume once Apex Feeds is reasonably satisfied that the relevant storage or handling concern has been corrected or otherwise resolved. A temporary restriction under this clause is a precautionary measure and does not, by itself, constitute termination of the Retailer’s Authorised Retailer status.</p>
<h4 id="s14-13">14.13 Cooperation and Corrective Action</h4>
<p>Where a genuine storage or handling issue is identified, Apex Feeds and the Retailer should reasonably cooperate to determine appropriate corrective action. Where the issue can reasonably be corrected through improved storage, replacement equipment, staff instruction, relocation of stock or another practical measure, the Retailer should be given a reasonable opportunity to address the issue unless immediate action is required to protect animal safety, product integrity or comply with law.</p>
<p>Repeated, deliberate or serious failure to maintain applicable product storage and handling requirements may be addressed under the breach, suspension and termination provisions of this Agreement.</p>
<h3 id="s15">15. Shelf-Stable Products</h3>
<p>Shelf-stable Apex Feeds products include dry, dehydrated, freeze-dried, powdered, supplementary and other products that do not require refrigerated or frozen storage prior to preparation or opening, as identified by the applicable product label or Apex Feeds product information. Shelf-stable products must be stored and handled in a manner that protects the product from moisture, contamination, excessive environmental exposure and deterioration throughout its retail life.</p>
<h4 id="s15-1">15.1 Storage Conditions</h4>
<p>Shelf-stable Apex Feeds products must be stored in clean, dry conditions appropriate to the product and in accordance with the applicable product label, Schedule A and any additional written instructions supplied by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Retailers must take reasonable precautions to protect shelf-stable products from:</p>
<ul>
<li>moisture and water exposure;</li>
<li>excessive humidity;</li>
<li>excessive heat;</li>
<li>prolonged direct sunlight where detrimental to the product;</li>
<li>pests and vermin;</li>
<li>chemical or environmental contamination; and</li>
<li>other conditions reasonably capable of compromising the product or its packaging.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id="s15-2">15.2 Moisture Protection</h4>
<p>Because moisture exposure may materially affect dehydrated, freeze-dried, powdered and other dry products, Retailers must take reasonable steps to maintain the integrity of the product’s packaging and moisture barrier. Products reasonably suspected of having been exposed to moisture through a puncture, failed seal, split packaging, water exposure or other packaging failure must be removed from sale and assessed in accordance with Section 19.</p>
<h4 id="s15-3">15.3 Packaging Condition</h4>
<p>Minor cosmetic packaging damage does not automatically make an Apex Feeds product unsuitable for sale. Products may remain available for sale where cosmetic damage does not affect the product, primary packaging seal, required product information or reasonable presentation of the product.</p>
<p>Products must be removed from normal sale where there is evidence of, or reasonable concern regarding: * punctured or split primary packaging;</p>
<ul>
<li>failed or broken seals;</li>
<li>water or moisture ingress;</li>
<li>visible mould or abnormal deterioration;</li>
<li>pest or insect contamination unrelated to the product’s intended contents;</li>
<li>unusual odour reasonably indicating deterioration or contamination;</li>
<li>leakage;</li>
<li>significant contamination of the packaging or product; or</li>
<li>another condition reasonably indicating that product integrity may have been compromised.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id="s15-4">15.4 Best Before Date and Batch Identification</h4>
<p>Shelf-stable Apex Feeds products will carry applicable Best Before Date and Batch Number identification, including where that information is applied to the product by label or sticker. Retailers must not intentionally remove, obscure, alter, replace or falsify the Best Before Date or Batch Number applied by Apex Feeds.</p>
<p>Where a Best Before Date or Batch Number sticker becomes damaged, detached or unreadable, the Retailer must not independently estimate or create replacement information. Where the original information can be reliably established, the Retailer should contact Apex Feeds for guidance or authorised replacement identification.</p>
<h4 id="s15-5">15.5 Stock Rotation</h4>
<p>Retailers should operate a first-expiring, first-out (FEFO) stock-rotation system so that products with the earliest Best Before Dates are ordinarily offered for sale before later-dated stock of the same product. Retailers remain responsible for checking stock dates and appropriately rotating Apex Feeds inventory. Detailed stock-rotation requirements are further addressed under Section 18.</p>
<h4 id="s15-6">15.6 Short-Dated Products</h4>
<p>A Retailer may continue selling an Apex Feeds product approaching its Best Before Date provided the product remains within its marked Best Before Date, has been appropriately stored and remains otherwise suitable for sale. The Retailer may independently discount or clear short-dated stock. Any such discount must be represented as a Retailer-established promotion in accordance with Sections 6 and 11. The Best Before Date must remain visible and must not be removed, altered or concealed for the purpose of facilitating the sale.</p>
<h4 id="s15-7">15.7 Products Beyond the Best Before Date</h4>
<p>Authorised Retailers must not offer an Apex Feeds product for retail sale after the marked Best Before Date has passed. Expired stock must be removed from saleable inventory and handled appropriately. The Retailer must not remove, replace or alter a Best Before Date for the purpose of extending the apparent retail life of a product.</p>
<h4 id="s15-8">15.8 Opened Store Stock</h4>
<p>Where a Retailer opens a shelf-stable Apex Feeds product for sampling, demonstration, staff education or another permitted store purpose, the opened product must not subsequently be sold or represented as a new, unopened or factory-sealed retail product.</p>
<p>Where the remaining product continues to be used for sampling, demonstration or internal purposes, it should be promptly resealed in its original suitable resealable packaging or transferred to an appropriate clean, dry and sealed container. The Retailer remains responsible for protecting opened product from moisture, contamination and deterioration.</p>
<h4 id="s15-9">15.9 Separation and Identification of Opened Stock</h4>
<p>Opened demonstration or sample stock should be reasonably distinguishable from unopened saleable inventory to reduce the risk of accidental retail sale. Where practical, Retailers are encouraged to record the date the product was opened, particularly where the product will continue to be used over an extended period. A formal opening log is not required unless Apex Feeds identifies a product-specific safety or quality reason for one.</p>
<h4 id="s15-10">15.10 Mixing of Batches</h4>
<p>Where Apex Feeds products are removed from their original packaging for permitted demonstration, sampling or internal use, Retailers should not combine or continually top up the same storage container with product from different Batch Numbers. Where practical, separate Batch Numbers should remain identifiable. This requirement supports product traceability and assists Apex Feeds and the Retailer in investigating any subsequent product-quality or safety concern.</p>
<h4 id="s15-11">15.11 Preparation and Rehydration</h4>
<p>Where a shelf-stable Apex Feeds product requires or permits the addition of water or another ingredient before feeding, the product’s shelf-stable status applies to the product before preparation. Once prepared, mixed or rehydrated, the resulting food must be handled and stored in accordance with the preparation, refrigeration, storage, feeding and disposal instructions applicable to that product. Retailers must not assume that the shelf life or storage conditions applicable to the original dry product continue to apply after preparation or rehydration.</p>
<h4 id="s15-12">15.12 Retailer-Prepared Samples</h4>
<p>Where a shelf-stable product is prepared or rehydrated for customer sampling, the requirements of Section 14.6 apply. The Retailer is responsible for appropriate hygiene, preparation, storage and distribution and for compliance with applicable Commonwealth, state or territory and local government requirements.</p>
<h4 id="s15-13">15.13 Returned Shelf-Stable Products</h4>
<p>An Apex Feeds food or feed product that has been opened after retail sale and subsequently returned by a customer must not be returned to normal saleable inventory or represented to another customer as a new product. The existence of a customer return does not, by itself, establish that the product is defective or create an entitlement to credit from Apex Feeds. Customer returns, product defects and Retailer claims against Apex Feeds are addressed separately under Sections 20–24.</p>
<h4 id="s15-14">15.14 Suspected Product Deterioration</h4>
<p>Where a Retailer identifies mould, unexpected moisture, abnormal deterioration, contamination or another condition that may indicate a product-quality issue, the affected stock should be removed from sale and the relevant Batch Number and Best Before Date retained. Where multiple units from the same Batch Number may be affected, the Retailer should take reasonable steps to identify and temporarily isolate the potentially affected stock pending further assessment.</p>
<p>The Retailer should contact Apex Feeds in accordance with the applicable claims or product-quality procedure rather than disposing of potentially relevant evidence unless immediate disposal is reasonably necessary for safety or required by law.</p>
<h3 id="s16">16. Frozen Products</h3>
<p>Frozen Apex Feeds products must be maintained under frozen storage conditions throughout their time under the Retailer’s possession or control. Retailers may use any freezer or frozen-storage system reasonably suitable for their premises provided it is capable of maintaining the required product-storage conditions. Apex Feeds does not prescribe a particular freezer type, manufacturer, configuration or commercial refrigeration system.</p>
<h4 id="s16-1">16.1 Frozen Storage Temperature</h4>
<p>Frozen Apex Feeds products should ordinarily be maintained at a temperature between approximately -10°C and -18°C. Apex Feeds currently maintains its own frozen products at approximately -14°C, however Retailers are not required to replicate Apex Feeds’ exact internal freezer setting. The Retailer is responsible for ensuring that its chosen freezer or storage system is capable of reliably maintaining Apex Feeds products in a frozen condition.</p>
<h4 id="s16-2">16.2 Continuous Frozen Storage</h4>
<p>Frozen Apex Feeds products are supplied and intended for retail sale as frozen products. Retailers must not deliberately thaw frozen Apex Feeds products for the purpose of displaying, storing or selling them as refrigerated or non-frozen products. Frozen products must be supplied to the end customer in a frozen condition except for incidental or partial softening that may reasonably occur during normal handling or transport.</p>
<h4 id="s16-3">16.3 Partial Thawing or Softening</h4>
<p>Minor or partial thawing, softening or temperature fluctuation does not automatically mean that a frozen Apex Feeds product is unsafe, defective or unsuitable for continued frozen storage. Where the product has remained appropriately cold and has not exceeded the temperature/time limits established under this Section, it may be returned promptly to appropriate frozen storage. The presence of some softening during freight or handling does not, by itself, establish a valid freight or product-quality claim.</p>
<h4 id="s16-4">16.4 Critical Temperature Exposure</h4>
<p>Where a frozen Apex Feeds product is known or reasonably believed to have exceeded 4°C for more than a brief period reasonably necessary for ordinary handling, loading, unloading or customer service, the affected product must be removed from sale and must not be supplied to customers.</p>
<p>Where the duration or extent of temperature exposure creates reasonable uncertainty regarding product suitability, the Retailer should quarantine the affected stock rather than assume it remains suitable for sale. Apex Feeds may request reasonable information regarding the circumstances of the temperature exposure when assisting the Retailer in assessing affected stock.</p>
<h4 id="s16-5">16.5 Disposal of Temperature-Abused Product</h4>
<p>Frozen product determined to have exceeded the acceptable temperature/time conditions under Section 16.4 must not be returned to retail sale. Affected stock must be appropriately disposed of and must not subsequently be refrozen for commercial sale. Where the stock may be relevant to a claim or investigation, the Retailer should retain applicable photographs, Batch Number, Best Before Date, quantity and other reasonably available evidence before disposal.</p>
<h4 id="s16-6">16.6 Freezer Failure</h4>
<p>Where a Retailer’s freezer fails or otherwise loses its ability to maintain appropriate frozen storage, the Retailer must take reasonable steps to protect the affected stock and restore suitable frozen conditions as quickly as practicable. A freezer malfunction does not automatically require disposal of all affected Apex Feeds stock. Where products remain sufficiently cold and have not exceeded the limits established under Section 16.4, they may be returned to appropriate frozen storage.</p>
<p>Where products have exceeded those limits, or where there is reasonable uncertainty concerning the extent of temperature exposure, the affected products must be removed from normal sale pending assessment or disposal. Loss resulting from failure of the Retailer’s freezer, electrical supply or other storage equipment will not ordinarily constitute a manufacturing or product-quality claim against Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s16-7">16.7 Refreezing</h4>
<p>A frozen Apex Feeds product that has experienced minor or partial softening but has remained within the acceptable temperature conditions established under this Section may be returned promptly to frozen storage. A product that has exceeded the temperature/time conditions established under Section 16.4 must not be refrozen for subsequent commercial sale. Retailers must not use refreezing as a means of returning temperature-compromised stock to saleable inventory.</p>
<h4 id="s16-8">16.8 Receipt of Frozen Deliveries</h4>
<p>Frozen deliveries must be inspected and transferred to appropriate frozen storage as soon as reasonably practicable following delivery. The Retailer should check the general condition of the shipment and identify any obvious evidence of significant thawing, packaging damage, leakage or other circumstances that may indicate product compromise.</p>
<p>Partial softening alone does not automatically constitute freight damage or product failure. Where a shipment presents reasonable concern regarding excessive temperature exposure, the Retailer should record available evidence and contact Apex Feeds promptly in accordance with the applicable freight and claims procedures.</p>
<h4 id="s16-9">16.9 Frozen Product Packaging</h4>
<p>Frozen products must remain in their original Apex Feeds retail packaging for retail sale unless Apex Feeds has specifically authorised another arrangement. Retailers must not intentionally remove or obscure applicable product identification, preparation information, storage information, Best Before Date or Batch Number.</p>
<h4 id="s16-10">16.10 Best Before Date and Batch Number</h4>
<p>Frozen Apex Feeds products will carry an identifiable Best Before Date and Batch Number, whether incorporated into the primary label or otherwise applied in an identifiable location on the product. Retailers must not intentionally remove, alter, obscure, replace or falsify this information. Where identification becomes damaged or unreadable, the Retailer should contact Apex Feeds rather than independently estimating or recreating the information.</p>
<h4 id="s16-11">16.11 Stock Rotation</h4>
<p>Frozen products should be rotated using a first-expiring, first-out (FEFO) approach. Products must not be offered for retail sale after their marked Best Before Date. Further general stock-rotation requirements are contained in Section 18.</p>
<h4 id="s16-12">16.12 Customer Transport</h4>
<p>Retailers should take reasonable steps to assist customers in maintaining frozen product condition during transport from the store. Retailers may determine the method most appropriate to their business and existing frozen-goods procedures.</p>
<p>Depending upon the circumstances, this may include wrapping frozen products in insulating paper, butcher’s paper, newspaper, insulated packaging, cold-storage packaging or another suitable method used by the Retailer for frozen goods.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds does not prescribe a particular customer transport method provided the Retailer’s approach is reasonable for the circumstances. Retailers should encourage customers to transport frozen products home promptly and return them to suitable frozen storage as soon as practicable.</p>
<h4 id="s16-13">16.13 Retailer Freezer Selection</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds does not require Retailers to purchase or operate any particular brand, model, value or style of freezer. Chest freezers, upright freezers, commercial display freezers and other suitable frozen-storage systems may be used provided they maintain appropriate frozen storage conditions and are suitable for the Retailer’s operation.</p>
<h4 id="s16-14">16.14 Frozen Product Displays</h4>
<p>Retailers must not remove frozen products from appropriate frozen storage merely for extended merchandising or display purposes. Where physical products cannot appropriately be displayed outside the freezer, Retailers may use approved photographs, signage, freezer graphics, product cards or other advertising material in accordance with Sections 10–13.</p>
<h4 id="s16-15">16.15 Suspected Frozen Product Quality Issues</h4>
<p>Where a Retailer identifies an issue with a frozen product that does not appear to have resulted from temperature exposure under the Retailer’s control, the affected product should be quarantined and the relevant Batch Number, Best Before Date and quantity recorded. Where practical, photographs and other relevant evidence should be retained and the matter reported through the applicable Apex Feeds claims procedure. Where multiple products from the same Batch Number may be affected, the Retailer should take reasonable steps to identify and temporarily isolate the relevant stock until further guidance is provided.</p>
<h3 id="s17">17. Live Feeders</h3>
<p>Apex Feeds aims to support Authorised Retailers in maintaining healthy, high-quality live feeder stock and will make reasonable husbandry and handling guidance available for live feeder species supplied through the wholesale program. Live feeders are living stock and require appropriate care following delivery.</p>
<p>Retailers are responsible for the ongoing husbandry, welfare, containment and lawful possession of live feeders while those animals remain under the Retailer’s possession or control. Apex Feeds recognises that established animal and reptile retailers may use different husbandry and retail systems.</p>
<p>Retailers are not required to replicate Apex Feeds’ own breeding, housing or holding systems provided their chosen methods appropriately maintain the live feeder species concerned and comply with applicable requirements.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds also recognises that live feeder insects are commercially different from its manufactured and packaged food, supplement and related product ranges. Accordingly, Authorised Retailers are provided greater flexibility in how live feeders are held, repacked, sold and used within their businesses, as set out below.</p>
<h4 id="s17-1">17.1 Inspection on Delivery</h4>
<p>Live feeder shipments must be inspected as soon as reasonably practicable following delivery. The Retailer should assess the general condition of the shipment and identify any abnormal mortality, significant packaging failure, escape, temperature-related concern or other obvious freight issue. Live feeders should not be unnecessarily left in freight cartons or transport conditions after delivery and should be transferred into appropriate holding conditions as soon as reasonably practicable.</p>
<h4 id="s17-2">17.2 Live Arrival Claims</h4>
<p>24 Hours</p>
<p>Any claim concerning abnormal mortality or the condition of live feeders on arrival must be reported to Apex Feeds within 24 hours of the carrier’s recorded delivery time.</p>
<p>The Retailer must provide reasonable supporting evidence, which may include:</p>
<ul>
<li>photographs or video of the affected live feeders;</li>
<li>photographs of the shipping container or packaging where relevant;</li>
<li>order or invoice information;</li>
<li>the feeder species and quantity affected;</li>
<li>the approximate extent of mortality or other issue; and</li>
<li>other information reasonably necessary to assess the claim.</li>
</ul>
<p>Photographs, videos and other evidence should be captured as close as reasonably practicable to the time the issue is identified. Where available, the date and time associated with photographic or video evidence may be considered when assessing the circumstances and timing of a claim. A claim first reported outside the 24-hour period may be declined where Apex Feeds can no longer reasonably distinguish between a freight or arrival-related issue and subsequent storage, environmental or husbandry conditions under the Retailer’s control. Nothing in this clause excludes any right or remedy that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
<h4 id="s17-3">17.3 Transfer to Appropriate Housing</h4>
<p>Following receipt and inspection, live feeders should be transferred into the Retailer’s appropriate live-food holding, storage or display system as soon as reasonably practicable. Retailers should avoid unnecessarily leaving live feeders in transport packaging where doing so may adversely affect ventilation, temperature, hydration, stocking conditions or general welfare.</p>
<h4 id="s17-4">17.4 Apex Feeds Husbandry Guidance</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may provide species-specific husbandry guidance covering matters such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>recommended temperature ranges;</li>
<li>ventilation;</li>
<li>hydration;</li>
<li>feeding;</li>
<li>gut-loading;</li>
<li>stocking density;</li>
<li>substrate;</li>
<li>cleaning;</li>
<li>containment; and</li>
<li>general maintenance.</li>
</ul>
<p>Detailed recommendations may be contained in Schedule A — Product Storage &amp; Handling Standards or other retailer husbandry resources supplied by Apex Feeds. These resources are intended to assist Retailers in maintaining healthy live feeder stock and may be updated as Apex Feeds’ husbandry practices, production experience and knowledge develop.</p>
<h4 id="s17-5">17.5 Retailer Husbandry Systems</h4>
<p>Retailers may use their own established tubs, racks, enclosures, heating systems, ventilation systems, feeding programs and other live-food husbandry methods. Apex Feeds does not require a Retailer to purchase or use particular equipment merely because that equipment or system is used internally by Apex Feeds. The Retailer’s chosen system must nevertheless be reasonably appropriate for the feeder species concerned and maintain suitable welfare, containment and stock condition.</p>
<h4 id="s17-6">17.6 Feeding, Hydration and Gut-Loading</h4>
<p>Retailers may determine the feeding, hydration and gut-loading program used for live feeders under their care. Retailers are not required to use Apex Feeds-branded gut-load, hydration or insect-feeding products as a condition of maintaining an Authorised Retailer account.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may recommend or supply products such as its gut-loads, insect foods or HydroBlu where appropriate, but Retailers remain free to use other suitable products and husbandry methods.</p>
<h4 id="s17-7">17.7 Routine Mortality and Stock Condition</h4>
<p>Some mortality may naturally occur when transporting and holding live feeder insects and does not automatically indicate a product defect or supply failure. Retailers should routinely monitor live feeder stock and take reasonable steps to remove excessive mortality, spoiled food, contamination and other material reasonably capable of adversely affecting the remaining stock.</p>
<p>Live feeders experiencing abnormal mortality, significant contamination or another condition reasonably indicating that the stock is unsuitable for retail supply should be removed from normal sale while the issue is assessed.</p>
<h4 id="s17-8">17.8 Husbandry Support</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds encourages Retailers experiencing difficulty maintaining an Apex Feeds live feeder species to contact Apex Feeds for reasonable husbandry guidance before the issue develops into significant stock loss.</p>
<p>Where appropriate, Apex Feeds may assist Retailers with troubleshooting matters such as environmental conditions, hydration, feeding, ventilation, stocking practices and general maintenance. Such assistance is intended to support the Retailer’s success in maintaining live feeder stock and does not transfer responsibility for the Retailer’s ongoing husbandry, equipment or livestock to Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s17-9">17.9 Breeding and Internal Use of Live Feeders</h4>
<p>Retailers may retain Apex Feeds live feeders for the purpose of establishing or maintaining their own feeder breeding colonies, feeding animals under their care or for other lawful purposes associated with the operation of their business. No separate permission from Apex Feeds is required for this purpose. Apex Feeds does not undertake to provide breeding instructions, breeding systems, commercial production methods or ongoing technical assistance for Retailer-operated breeding programs. Where requested and commercially available, Apex Feeds may supply appropriate gut-load, hydration and other insect-husbandry products to support the Retailer’s own breeding or holding operations.</p>
<h4 id="s17-10">17.10 Bulk Live Feeder Orders and Retail Repacking</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may make bulk quantities of live feeders available to Authorised Retailers, including custom or larger-volume orders intended to assist Retailers in managing their own live feeder inventory and retail pack sizes.</p>
<p>Authorised Retailers may divide bulk live feeder quantities into smaller retail quantities for sale to end customers. For example, a Retailer purchasing a bulk quantity of Mealworms may divide that stock into smaller tubs or containers appropriate to the Retailer’s customer demand.</p>
<p>Retailers may determine their own retail pack sizes, quantities, containers and retail pricing for live feeders repacked from bulk Apex Feeds live stock. Where live feeders are independently repacked by the Retailer, the Retailer remains responsible for the accuracy of the quantity, packaging, labelling, condition and presentation of those individual retail packs.</p>
<p>Retailer-packed containers must not falsely represent that the individual container was weighed, packed, sealed or individually quality-controlled by Apex Feeds where that work was performed by the Retailer.</p>
<h4 id="s17-11">17.11 Commercial Use of Live Feeders</h4>
<p>Subject to applicable law and this Agreement, Authorised Retailers are generally free to determine how live feeders purchased from Apex Feeds are incorporated into their business.</p>
<p>Permitted ordinary commercial uses may include:</p>
<ul>
<li>resale in the original supplied quantity;</li>
<li>division of bulk quantities into smaller retail quantities;</li>
<li>creation of Retailer-selected live feeder pack sizes;</li>
<li>bulk sale to end customers;</li>
<li>feeding to animals;</li>
<li>gut-loading prior to sale or use;</li>
<li>holding live feeders for future sale; and</li>
<li>establishing or maintaining feeder breeding colonies.</li>
</ul>
<p>The restrictions elsewhere in this Agreement concerning alteration, division, repackaging or unauthorised manufacture of Apex Feeds’ manufactured food, supplement and other packaged product ranges must not be interpreted as preventing the ordinary commercial use and repacking of live feeder insects permitted under this Section.</p>
<h4 id="s17-12">17.12 Distinction From Manufactured Apex Feeds Products</h4>
<p>The flexibility provided under Sections 17.9–17.11 applies specifically to live feeder insects. Unless separately authorised by Apex Feeds, it does not permit a Retailer to divide, repackage, relabel, reformulate or manufacture new retail pack sizes or products from Apex Feeds’ manufactured food, supplement, prepared feed, hydration, gut-load or other packaged product ranges and represent those resulting products as Apex Feeds retail products.</p>
<p>For clarity, purchasing bulk live Mealworms and dividing those Mealworms into smaller retail tubs is permitted under this Section. Purchasing a bulk quantity of an Apex Feeds manufactured food or supplement and independently dividing it into smaller Apex Feeds-branded retail packs is not permitted unless Apex Feeds has specifically authorised that arrangement.</p>
<h4 id="s17-13">17.13 Bulk Gut-Load, HydroBlu and Husbandry Products</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may supply bulk gut-load, HydroBlu or other insect-husbandry products to Authorised Retailers for use within their own live feeder operations, including where the Retailer maintains or breeds feeder insects. Unless specifically authorised by Apex Feeds, the supply of a bulk manufactured Apex Feeds product does not give the Retailer authority to divide that product into smaller quantities and sell those quantities as independently packaged Apex Feeds products.</p>
<p>Bulk manufactured products may be used internally by the Retailer in accordance with their intended purpose. Nothing in this clause prevents Apex Feeds from establishing separately approved bulk, private-label, retailer-packed or other commercial arrangements in writing where Apex Feeds chooses to do so.</p>
<h4 id="s17-14">17.14 Biosecurity and Legal Requirements</h4>
<p>Retailers are responsible for ensuring that their possession, keeping, breeding, sale and movement of live feeder species complies with applicable Commonwealth, state or territory and local requirements, including any applicable biosecurity, pest, animal-welfare, movement or keeping restrictions.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds will also take reasonable steps not to knowingly supply a live feeder species into a jurisdiction where Apex Feeds is aware that the relevant supply is prohibited. Where uncertainty exists regarding the lawful supply of a particular feeder species into a jurisdiction, Apex Feeds may decline or temporarily hold the relevant order while the position is clarified.</p>
<h4 id="s17-15">17.15 Containment and Escape Prevention</h4>
<p>Retailers must maintain reasonable containment appropriate to the feeder species concerned. Live feeders must not knowingly be housed, handled or displayed in a manner that creates an unreasonable risk of escape, infestation or contamination of other stock. The Retailer remains responsible for the management of escaped live feeders occurring after successful delivery into its possession or control.</p>
<h4 id="s17-16">17.16 Customer Information</h4>
<p>Retailers are encouraged to provide customers with reasonable information concerning the appropriate short-term care, feeding, hydration and storage of live feeders where relevant. Retailers may provide this information using Apex Feeds husbandry material, their own husbandry knowledge or a combination of both, subject to the product representation requirements contained in Section 12.</p>
<h4 id="s17-17">17.17 Ongoing Responsibility Following Delivery</h4>
<p>Once live feeders have been successfully delivered and the applicable 24-hour live-arrival claim period has passed, deterioration or mortality resulting from the Retailer’s subsequent environmental conditions, husbandry, feeding, hydration, equipment failure, containment or other circumstances under the Retailer’s control will not ordinarily constitute a claim against Apex Feeds. This does not prevent Apex Feeds from assisting the Retailer in identifying and correcting a husbandry issue or otherwise providing reasonable support.</p>
<h3 id="s18">18. Stock Rotation &amp; Expiry</h3>
<p>Authorised Retailers are responsible for reasonable stock rotation and inventory management of Apex Feeds products held for retail sale. Apex Feeds will take reasonable steps to supply products with an appropriate remaining saleable life having regard to the nature of the product, its total shelf life and normal retail turnover. Apex Feeds does not guarantee a fixed minimum remaining shelf life unless a particular minimum has been expressly agreed for a product, order or promotion.</p>
<h4 id="s18-1">18.1 Best Before Date and Batch Identification</h4>
<p>Where applicable, Apex Feeds products will carry an identifiable Best Before Date (BBD) and Batch Number (BN). This information may form part of the primary product label or may be separately applied to the product in another clearly identifiable location. Retailers must not intentionally remove, alter, obscure, replace or falsify a Best Before Date or Batch Number.</p>
<h4 id="s18-2">18.2 First Expiring, First Out</h4>
<p>Retailers should manage Apex Feeds inventory using a First Expiring, First Out (FEFO) approach wherever reasonably practicable. Products with an earlier Best Before Date should ordinarily be offered for sale before otherwise equivalent stock carrying a later Best Before Date. Retailers remain responsible for the day-to-day rotation of stock within their stores, storage areas and other authorised sales locations.</p>
<h4 id="s18-3">18.3 Stock Received From Apex Feeds</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds will take reasonable steps to avoid supplying stock that does not have an appropriate remaining period for ordinary retail sale. What constitutes an appropriate remaining saleable life may vary according to the product type, total expected shelf life, storage requirements, production cycle, order quantity and other relevant circumstances. A fixed minimum remaining shelf life does not apply across the entire Apex Feeds range unless Apex Feeds has expressly stated otherwise for a particular product or arrangement.</p>
<h4 id="s18-4">18.4 Short-Dated Stock</h4>
<p>A product approaching its Best Before Date does not automatically become defective, compromised or unsuitable for retail sale. Provided the product remains within its marked Best Before Date, has been correctly stored and remains otherwise suitable for sale, the Retailer may continue offering the product for sale. Retailers may independently reduce the retail price, place the product on clearance, include it in a promotion or otherwise manage short-dated inventory in accordance with Sections 6 and 11. The applicable Best Before Date must remain visible and must not be misrepresented to the customer.</p>
<h4 id="s18-5">18.5 Specifically Disclosed Short-Dated Stock</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds may occasionally offer stock that has a shorter than usual remaining saleable life at a reduced wholesale price, as clearance stock or under another special commercial arrangement. Where the shortened remaining shelf life is material to the purchasing decision, Apex Feeds will disclose that circumstance before or at the time the Retailer agrees to purchase the affected stock. Stock knowingly purchased under such an arrangement is not defective merely because of the disclosed remaining Best Before period.</p>
<h4 id="s18-6">18.6 Products Past Best Before Date</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds products must not be offered for retail sale after their marked Best Before Date has passed. Expired stock must be removed from normal retail inventory and appropriately separated from saleable stock pending disposal or other lawful use. A Retailer must not alter, replace or remove the Best Before Date for the purpose of extending the apparent retail life of a product.</p>
<h4 id="s18-7">18.7 Expiry While Under Retailer Control</h4>
<p>A product does not become the responsibility of Apex Feeds merely because it becomes short-dated or reaches its Best Before Date while held in the Retailer’s inventory. Where Apex Feeds supplied the product with an appropriate remaining saleable life and the product subsequently expires because of Retailer ordering quantities, turnover, stock rotation or inventory management, the resulting stock loss will not ordinarily qualify for return, refund or wholesale credit. This does not apply where Apex Feeds supplied stock in circumstances inconsistent with an expressly agreed shelf-life requirement or failed to disclose a material short-dated condition that should reasonably have been disclosed.</p>
<h4 id="s18-8">18.8 Stock Rotation Between Deliveries</h4>
<p>Where a new Apex Feeds delivery is received while the Retailer still holds stock of the same product, the Retailer should check applicable Best Before Dates rather than assuming the newly delivered stock should automatically be placed behind or ahead of existing inventory. Stock should be rotated according to the actual Best Before Dates shown on the products.</p>
<h4 id="s18-9">18.9 Damaged or Unreadable Date Identification</h4>
<p>Where a Best Before Date or Batch Number becomes detached, damaged or unreadable, the Retailer must not independently estimate, recreate or substitute that information. Where the correct information can be reliably established, the Retailer may contact Apex Feeds for guidance or authorised replacement identification. Where the product cannot be reliably identified and its saleability cannot reasonably be established, it should be removed from normal retail sale.</p>
<h4 id="s18-10">18.10 Slow-Moving Stock</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds encourages Retailers to contact Apex Feeds where particular products are consistently experiencing low turnover or approaching their Best Before Dates before being sold. Where appropriate, Apex Feeds may assist the Retailer with product information, merchandising suggestions, customer education, promotional material or future ordering quantities. Such assistance does not guarantee the sale of the Retailer’s inventory or transfer responsibility for normal inventory management to Apex Feeds.</p>
<h4 id="s18-11">18.11 Product-Specific Requirements</h4>
<p>Certain products may require additional stock-rotation, storage or expiry controls because of their formulation, packaging or product type. Any such requirements may be specified on the product label, in Schedule A — Product Storage &amp; Handling Standards, or in other written product information supplied by Apex Feeds. Where a product-specific requirement is more restrictive than the general requirements of this Section, the product-specific requirement applies.</p>
<h3 id="s19">19. Damaged or Compromised Stock</h3>
<p>Where an Apex Feeds product is damaged, contaminated, deteriorated or otherwise reasonably suspected of being unsuitable for retail sale, the Retailer must take reasonable steps to prevent the affected product from being supplied to customers until its condition has been assessed.</p>
<p>The purpose of this Section is to protect customers, animals, Retailers and Apex Feeds while allowing genuine product concerns to be investigated fairly and efficiently. The identification or quarantine of a product under this Section does not, by itself, establish that the product is defective or that Apex Feeds is responsible for the condition.</p>
<h4 id="s19-1">19.1 Identification of Potentially Compromised Stock</h4>
<p>A product should be removed from normal retail sale where there are reasonable grounds to suspect that its quality, safety, packaging or integrity has been materially compromised.</p>
<p>Circumstances may include: |</p>
<ul>
<li>mould, abnormal deterioration or unexpected spoilage;</li>
<li>significant moisture or water exposure;</li>
<li>contamination or suspected contamination;</li>
<li>pest contamination;</li>
<li>punctured, split, leaking or materially failed packaging;</li>
<li>abnormal odour, appearance or condition inconsistent with the product;</li>
<li>significant frozen-product temperature exposure contrary to Section 16;</li>
<li>abnormal mortality or condition of live feeders;</li>
<li>chemical or foreign-material exposure;</li>
<li>storage or equipment failure affecting product integrity;</li>
<li>missing or unreadable essential product identification where suitability cannot otherwise be established; or</li>
<li>another circumstance giving the Retailer reasonable grounds to question whether the product remains suitable for sale.</li>
</ul>
<p>Minor cosmetic damage to outer packaging does not automatically make a product compromised where the product itself, its primary packaging, required information and overall saleability remain unaffected.</p>
<h4 id="s19-2">19.2 Immediate Removal From Sale</h4>
<p>Where a Retailer reasonably suspects that a product may be materially compromised, the affected product must be removed from normal retail sale as soon as reasonably practicable. Where appropriate, the Retailer should also temporarily remove or isolate other affected units where there are reasonable grounds to believe they may be subject to the same issue.</p>
<p>The Retailer should not continue selling affected stock merely because the cause of the issue has not yet been established.</p>
<h4 id="s19-3">19.3 Quarantine</h4>
<p>Affected stock should be clearly separated or otherwise identified so that it cannot accidentally be returned to sale while the issue is being assessed. Quarantine does not require a particular physical quarantine room or specialised facility.</p>
<p>A reasonable system appropriate to the Retailer’s premises may be used provided the affected stock is clearly identifiable and protected from accidental sale or use. Products requiring frozen or other specialised storage must continue to be maintained under appropriate storage conditions while quarantined unless disposal is required for immediate safety reasons.</p>
<h4 id="s19-4">19.4 Product Identification and Evidence</h4>
<p>Where reasonably available, the Retailer should record and retain information relevant to the affected product, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>product name;</li>
<li>quantity affected;</li>
<li>Batch Number (BN);</li>
<li>Best Before Date (BBD);</li>
<li>photographs or video showing the issue;</li>
<li>relevant order or invoice details;</li>
<li>date the issue was identified; and</li>
<li>a brief description of the circumstances.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where freight packaging, cartons, insulation or other shipping materials may be relevant to the issue, the Retailer should also retain reasonable photographic evidence before those materials are discarded.</p>
<h4 id="s19-5">19.5 Contacting Apex Feeds</h4>
<p>Where the issue may reasonably involve a manufacturing defect, packaging failure, contamination, freight issue, broader batch concern or other matter potentially attributable to Apex Feeds or its supply chain, the Retailer should notify Apex Feeds in accordance with the applicable claims procedure.</p>
<p>Urgent product-safety or animal-safety concerns should be reported to Apex Feeds as soon as reasonably practicable rather than waiting for the ordinary claims process. Applicable reporting periods for particular claim types, including live feeder arrival claims, remain governed by the relevant provisions of this Agreement.</p>
<h4 id="s19-6">19.6 Do Not Dispose of Relevant Evidence Prematurely</h4>
<p>Where a Retailer intends to make a claim concerning affected stock, the product and relevant packaging should not ordinarily be discarded until Apex Feeds has had a reasonable opportunity to assess the information and advise whether the product needs to be retained, returned or disposed of.</p>
<p>Apex Feeds may request photographs, video, product identification or physical return of affected stock where reasonably necessary to assess a claim. This requirement does not prevent immediate disposal where retaining the product would create an unreasonable health, safety, contamination or biosecurity risk or where disposal is otherwise required by law. Where immediate disposal is necessary, the Retailer should preserve reasonable photographic and identification evidence where practicable.</p>
<h4 id="s19-7">19.7 Assessment of Affected Stock</h4>
<p>Depending on the nature of the issue, Apex Feeds may reasonably advise that affected stock:</p>
<ul>
<li>remains suitable for sale;</li>
<li>should remain quarantined pending further assessment;</li>
<li>should be returned to Apex Feeds;</li>
<li>should be disposed of;</li>
<li>requires replacement, credit or another remedy where applicable; or</li>
<li>forms part of a broader product withdrawal or recall process.</li>
</ul>
<p>Apex Feeds will take reasonable account of the product type, available evidence, Batch Number, storage history, freight circumstances and other relevant information when assessing the issue.</p>
<h4 id="s19-8">19.8 Retailer-Controlled Damage or Deterioration</h4>
<p>Damage or deterioration caused after successful delivery by circumstances under the Retailer’s control will not ordinarily constitute a manufacturing defect or claim against Apex Feeds. This may include damage resulting from inappropriate storage, excessive heat, moisture, freezer failure, contamination, pest exposure, mishandling, failure to follow applicable storage requirements or other Retailer-controlled circumstances. Apex Feeds may nevertheless provide reasonable assistance in determining whether affected stock remains suitable or in preventing a similar issue from recurring.</p>
<h4 id="s19-9">19.9 Accidental Damage</h4>
<p>Where an otherwise satisfactory product is accidentally damaged by the Retailer or its staff—for example through dropping, cutting, crushing, puncturing or otherwise damaging the packaging—the product should be assessed according to its actual condition. Apex Feeds is not ordinarily responsible for replacing or crediting stock damaged after delivery through Retailer handling. Where the damage compromises the product’s integrity or makes it unsuitable for sale, it must be removed from normal retail inventory.</p>
<h4 id="s19-10">19.10 Customer-Damaged or Returned Products</h4>
<p>Products returned by customers in an opened, used, contaminated, improperly stored or otherwise compromised condition must not be returned to normal sale as new product. The existence of a customer return does not, by itself, establish that the product was defective when originally supplied. Customer returns and subsequent Retailer claims against Apex Feeds are dealt with further under Sections 20–24.</p>
<h4 id="s19-11">19.11 Suspected Batch-Wide Issue</h4>
<p>Where multiple products carrying the same Batch Number display the same or a substantially similar unexpected issue, the Retailer should notify Apex Feeds promptly. Where reasonably practicable, potentially affected stock from the relevant Batch Number should be temporarily identified or isolated while Apex Feeds assesses whether the concern appears limited to individual units or may involve a broader batch. The Retailer must cooperate reasonably with any subsequent traceability, withdrawal or recall process under Sections 26 and 27.</p>
<h4 id="s19-12">19.12 No Unauthorised Alteration to Restore Saleability</h4>
<p>A Retailer must not attempt to make materially compromised stock saleable by altering packaging, replacing product identification, changing a Best Before Date, removing evidence of contamination or deterioration, combining affected product with unaffected product, or otherwise concealing the condition of the stock. This does not prevent ordinary minor maintenance of retail presentation that does not affect the product itself or misrepresent its condition.</p>
<h4 id="s19-13">19.13 Precautionary Quarantine Is Not a Finding of Defect</h4>
<p>A request by Apex Feeds for a Retailer to temporarily quarantine or stop selling particular stock is a precautionary product-control measure and does not constitute an admission that the product is defective, unsafe or subject to a manufacturing failure. Where an investigation determines that quarantined stock remains suitable for sale, Apex Feeds may advise the Retailer that the stock can be returned to normal inventory.</p>
<h4 id="s19-14">19.14 Cooperation and Resolution</h4>
<p>Apex Feeds and the Retailer should cooperate reasonably to identify the cause and appropriate resolution of genuine stock-quality concerns. The Retailer must provide information reasonably necessary to assess the affected stock, while Apex Feeds will provide reasonable guidance regarding assessment, return, disposal, replacement, credit or other appropriate action. Nothing in this Section limits any right or remedy that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>

